\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro steady against dollar as ECB rates on hold. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Carolyn Cohn \par \uc2 637 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 November 2000\par 14:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Nov 16 (Reuters) - The euro barely moved against the dollar on Thursday after the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  left interest rates unchanged, as expected. \par \par \uc2  The main market focus remained on the indecisive U.S. election and the possibility of ECB \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, political uncertainty in \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued to sour sentiment towards the yen, which traded within a whisker of two-week lows against the dollar set on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  ECB board member Eugenio Domingo Solans kept the threat of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  alive after he said on Wednesday that an undervalued \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  risked both credibility and stability. The ECB has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on three days in the past two weeks. \par \par \uc2  The prospect of more \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action, rather than the ECB's decision on Thursday to leave its benchmark minimum bid rate unchanged at 4.75 percent, was therefore under the spotlight. \par \par \uc2  "The market is looking for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , not a rate hike," said Sonja Hellemann, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Dresdner Kleinwort Benson in London. \par \par \uc2  The euro was hovering around $0.8565 EUR=) at 1250 GMT, according to Reuters data, at the lower end of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's half-cent range for the day. \par \par \uc2  Any new developments in the U.S. election process were likely to affect the euro/dollar cross rate, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  Initial losses the euro suffered after Wednesday's decision by Florida's state secretary to disallow hand counted votes delivered after the deadline were recouped as Democrats said they would contest the decision in court. \par \par \uc2  The Florida state secretary's decision was seen favouring Bush and initially helped the dollar, as a Bush administration is expected to be less inclined to join in coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the euro. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. Federal Reserve, meanwhile, also left interest rates on hold on Wednesday, as expected. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar outlook is overshadowed by the election at the moment," said Matthew Clements, economist at Prebon Marshall Yamane in London. \par \par \uc2  The euro proved resilient to data showing German wholesale price inflation reached a higher than expected 7.4 percent year-on-year in October, its highest rate for 18 years. \par \par \uc2  U.S. consumer price data are due at 1330 GMT, and are forecast to have risen by 0.2 percent in October from the previous month. \par \par \uc2  YEN EYES BREAK OF RANGE \par \par \uc2  The dollar capitalised on political uncertainty in Japan, rising close to crucial technical resistance at 109. \par \par \uc2  The position of deeply unpopular Prime Minister Yoshiro Mori looked increasingly precarious on Thursday, as jockeying went on within the ruling Liberal Democratic Party to replace him. \par \par \uc2  "The market is not so much concerned about political change but that there could be a political vacuum," said Steven Saywell, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at Fuji Bank in London. \par \par \uc2  "The 105-110 range we have seen is likely to be tested to the topside." \par \par \uc2  The dollar has been confined to a a five-yen range against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for much of this year. \par \par \uc2  By 1300 GMT, the dollar was trading at the day's highs around 108.90 yen JPY=), a shade below the previous day's two-week highs. \par \par \uc2  Sterling fluctuated in response to British data and to talk of merger and acquisition-related \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  flows. \par \par \uc2  The pound recovered from earlier one-week lows against the dollar after retail sales remained unchanged in October from the previous month after expectations for a 0.2 percent fall. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of England's quarterly inflation report, meanwhile, reinforced the increasingly prevailing view that British interest rates have peaked. The Bank forecast underlying inflation would be around the government's 2.5 percent target in two years' time. \par \par \uc2  Sterling was trading around $1.4235 GBP=) and 60.15 pence per euro EURGBP=) at 1300 GMT, around the middle of the day's ranges. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010822dwbg01v69\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
