\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro supported against dollar, yen mired. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Carolyn Cohn \par \uc2 601 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 November 2000\par 13:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Nov 16 (Reuters) - The euro nudged higher against the dollar on Thursday, as potentially euro-bearish developments in the U.S. election were outweighed by wariness of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's support. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, political uncertainty in \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued to sour sentiment towards the yen, which was mired within a whisker of two-week lows against the dollar it had set on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Initial losses which the euro suffered after Florida's state secretary on Wednesday disallowed hand counted votes delivered after the deadline were recouped as Democrats said they would contest the decision in court. \par \par \uc2  The euro was also supported before the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  holds its regular policy meeting on Thursday. While no change in interest rates is expected, dealers were wary it could mark the occasion by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 , analysts said. \par \par \uc2  ECB board member Eugenio Domingo Solans kept the threat of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  alive after he said on Wednesday that an undervalued \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  risked both credibility and stability. The ECB has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on three days in the past two weeks. \par \par \uc2  "The downside for the euro has been limited by fear of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Steven Saywell, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at Fuji Bank in London. \par \par \uc2  The euro was hovering around $0.8585 at 1030 GMT, according to Reuters data, up from lows below $0.8560 set in New York in the wake of the decision by the Florida state secretary. \par \par \uc2  Her decision was seen favouring Bush and initially helped the dollar, as a Bush administration is expected to be less inclined to join in coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the euro. \par \par \uc2  Political wrangling, rather than the Federal Reserve's widely-expected decision to leave key U.S. interest rates unchanged on Wednesday, gave the dollar its direction. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar outlook is overshadowed by the election at the moment," said Matthew Clements, economist at Prebon Marshall Yamane in London. \par \par \uc2  The euro proved resilient to data showing German wholesale price inflation reached a higher than expected 7.4 percent year-on-year in October, its highest rate for 18 years. \par \par \uc2  POLITICAL UNCERTAINTY IN JAPAN \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the dollar capitalised on political uncertainty in Japan, rising to within spitting distance of crucial technical resistance at 109. \par \par \uc2  The position of deeply unpopular Prime Minister Yoshiro Mori looked increasingly precarious on Thursday, as jockeying went on within the ruling Liberal Democratic Party to have him replaced. \par \par \uc2  "The market is not so much concerned about political change, but that there could be a political vacuum," said Saywell. \par \par \uc2  "The 105-110 range we have seen is likely to be tested to the topside." \par \par \uc2  The dollar has been confined to a a five-yen range against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for much of this year. \par \par \uc2  By 1030 GMT, the dollar was trading at the day's highs around 108.90 yen, a shade below the previous day's two-week highs. \par \par \uc2  Sterling was the main mover in largely stagnant markets, traders said, as it fluctuated in response to British data and to talk of merger and acquisition-related \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  flows. \par \par \uc2  The pound recovered from earlier one-week lows against the dollar after retail sales remained unchanged in October from the previous month, above expectations for a 0.2 percent fall. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of England's quarterly inflation report, meanwhile, reinforced the increasingly prevailing view that British interest rates have peaked. The Bank forecast underlying inflation would be around the government's 2.5 percent target in two years' time. \par \par \uc2  Sterling was trading around $1.4250 and 60.20 pence per euro at 1045 GMT, around the middle of the day's ranges. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010822dwbg01uou\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
