\par\par \b \uc2  INTERVIEW:Ex-MOF Nakahira: US  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  Policy To Remain Intact \b0\par\par\uc2  By Hidenobu Kageyama \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \uc2 353 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 November 2000\par 12:31\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- The U.S. is not expected to alter its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy or \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategies no matter what political changes occur, a former Japanese Finance Ministry official said Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Even if Bush were to win the presidential election, "I don't think the U.S.'s \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy will change much," former vice finance minister for international affairs Kosuke Nakahira told Dow Jones in an interview. \par \par \uc2  Nakahira, currently the vice chairman of the Institute for International Economic Studies, a private research institution, was speaking as U.S. media were predicting a Bush victory in a very close race. \par \par \uc2  He stressed that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy of the U.S. would remain intact even if Bush were elected. The U.S. still believes an overly weak euro is not in its interests, Nakahira said. \par \par \uc2  "If the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  asks the U.S. authorities to jointly take action against the euro's weakness, the U.S. wouldn't reject the request," he said. \par \par \uc2  Bush's chief financial advisor Lawrence Lindsey, who is widely expected to take a top economic post if Bush becomes president, spoke out against the U.S.'s participation in September's round of coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the euro. Nakahira said the remarks reflected partisan posturing rather than a genuine difference in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy with Bill Clinton's administration. \par \par \uc2  "Lindsey criticized what U.S. Treasury Secretary Lawrence Summers did, during the election campaign. But the GOP will flexibly take action in markets, as a weak euro is regarded as a negative factor for the U.S. economy," Nakahira said. \par \par \uc2  Nakahira said that Bush wouldn't be eager to abandon the strong dollar policy. \par \par \uc2  He added that he expects Japanese authorities to maintain their stance towards the European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Although \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  won't always jointly \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  with the ECB to support\par the euro, an excessively weak euro is definitely not in Japan's\par interest," he said.\par   -By Hidenobu Kageyama, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929;\par hidenobu.kageyama@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dwb805dkq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
