\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 2-Japan spent $1.3 bln to prop up euro in Sept. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Masayuki Kitano \par \uc2 581 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 November 2000\par 07:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Nov 8 (Reuters) - Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) said on Wednesday it spent 143.5 billion yen ($1.34 billion) buying the beleaguered euro in joint \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  with other Group of Seven nations in September. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the amount confirmed Japan's determination to help prop up the weak euro, long a source of pain for its investors and businesses in Europe. \par \par \uc2  The $1.3 billion figure was in line with initial estimates of how much the Finance Ministry, acting through the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , had used in the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  - about half that estimated to have been spent by the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (ECB) and around the same as the U.S. Federal Reserve. \par \par \uc2  "It may not be an exact match...but it is mostly in line with what the market had expected," said Taisuke Tanaka, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist for Credit Suisse First Boston (CSFB) in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  The surprise joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which was also supported by other G7 central banks, took place on September 22, two days after the euro fell to a then record low of $0.8440. \par \par \uc2  It succeeded in pushing the euro up briefly, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  quickly ceded those gains and the ECB was forced into a lone \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on its behalf last week. \par \par \uc2  The ECB is estimated to have bought 3.0 billion euros ($2.6 billion) to 5.0 billion euros and the United States to have spent some $1.3 billion in the joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  effort. \par \par \uc2  So far, Britain has confirmed that it purchased 85 million euros against sterling while Canada has said it spent $97 million to buy euros. \par \par \uc2  The MOF figures were released as part of the ministry's quarterly disclosure of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  amounts along with data on \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's foreign reserves, which rose to a record high $349.055 billion at the end of October. \par \par \uc2  In the April-June quarter, Japan spent 1.385 trillion yen on dollar-buying, yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Since then, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's concern has shifted from the yen's strength against the dollar to the euro's relentless decline, which has hit the yen value of Japanese investments and business profits in Europe. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2  SWAP WITH ECB \par \par \uc2  The foreign reserves data also showed that the amount of short positions in forwards and futures in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the yen stood at $1.273 billion in October. \par \par \uc2  MOF and BOJ officials have said the figure reflects a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap between the Bank of Japan and the ECB, which analysts think was conducted to fund ECB buying of the euro with yen on September 22. \par \par \uc2  Through the transaction, the BOJ effectively lent the ECB around 136 billion yen which it then used to buy euros, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  The disclosed amount of the BOJ's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on September 22 and the size of its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap transaction with the ECB was consistent with estimates placing the total amount of G7 \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at around six billion euros, said CSFB's Tanaka. \par \par \uc2  Assuming the ECB used all of the yen it borrowed via the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap for its September 22 \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it suggests the ECB may have conducted about half of its euro-buying against the yen and half against the dollar, he said. \par \par \uc2  The ECB is reticent about how much it spends on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and has not provided clear figures for the volume of its September 22 buying. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010822dwb802j1b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
