\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Dollar Immobile Vs Yen As US Election Looms \b0\par\par\uc2  By Miyako Takebe \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \uc2 805 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 November 2000\par 06:30\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- The dollar was static against the yen in Asia Tuesday, as the impending U.S. presidential election later in the global day left Tokyo players with no choice but to retreat to the sidelines and await the results. \par \par \uc2  The dollar found itself unable to break out of an extremely tight 15-sen range against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and stayed locked between Y107.33-Y107.48 in lethargic trading. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the euro managed to stay afloat against both the dollar and the yen despite an early test of its downside, as recent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was effective - if not in boosting - in providing a floor to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Regarding the upcoming election, most Tokyo market players agreed that regardless of the outcome, there would not be much general or immediate change to U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy in favor of a stronger dollar. \par \par \uc2  "Although we are not completely without views on the possibility of what will happen if Bush wins, or if Gore wins, its very hard for us in Japan to accurately gauge what impact the outcome will have on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, as we are so removed from the U.S. (political scene)," said Minoru Shioiri, manager of the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at Kokusai Securities. \par \par \uc2  "But in any case, there is unlikely to be any immediate or sudden change to U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy," he said. \par \par \uc2  The fact that the race is expected to be extremely close has also eliminated the surprise factor, as the market has already factored in both possibilities, traders said. \par \par \uc2  "What can be said is that as a rule, trading in the aftermath of a U.S. election tends to pick up, so hopefully the dollar will gather enough incentive to break out of its range and start moving around this time Wednesday," said Kokusai's Shiori. \par \par \uc2  However, a Japanese bank trader noted that "aside from position adjustments, there is unlikely to be a sudden emergence of a new trend in dollar/yen trading." \par \par \uc2  At 0515 GMT (12:15 a.m. EST), the dollar was quoted at Y107.45, little changed from Y107.48 late Monday in New York. The dollar was at Y107.19 late Monday in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at $0.8627, higher than $0.8619 late Monday in New York. The euro was at $0.8659 in Tokyo Monday. \par \par \uc2  Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y92.69, up slightly from Y92.60 in New York late Monday. The euro was at Y92.82 in Tokyo late Monday. \par \par \uc2  The euro remained stable against the dollar, recovering from an early dip to $0.8613 on fears that the ECB will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  yet again later in the global day, as was the case on Monday. \par \par \uc2  "As the ECB's past \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  action has come in near $0.8600, traders are starting to fall under the impression that there will be more \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the euro drops below that level," said Kokusai's Shioiri. \par \par \uc2  Japanese authorities, including Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa, Tuesday acknowledged recent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the ECB as being in line with the Group of Seven policy on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  "The ECB may have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to capitalize on narrowing growth differentials and an apparent change in capital flows between the U.S. and the euro-zone countries. Anyway, (the action) was in line with the G7 accord reached at the meeting in Prague," Miyazawa told a regular press conference. \par \par \uc2  Economic Planning Agency Director-General Taichi Sakaiya said Tuesday that as \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has longed hoped for the euro to stabilize, ECB \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  which has brought the euro to levels near Y92.00 against the yen has been "appropriate." \par \par \uc2  But Kokusai's Shioiri noted that while the ECB may be able to keep market players wary for a short while, all it has effectively done is "buy the euro some time." \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is only able to address short-term supply and demand factors, and unless European authorities are able to deal with fundamental issues and make Europe a more attractive market for investors, there will be no shift in the trend toward a weaker euro, he said. \par \par \uc2  Late in Tokyo Tuesday, sterling was at $1.4292, up from $1.4288 in New York Monday and higher than $1.4472 in Tokyo Monday. \par \par \uc2  -By Miyako Takebe, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; miyako.takebe@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  The chart of late Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates which accompanied Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been replaced with an enhanced \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixture which is updated hourly. \par \par \uc2  Subscribers can find this table: \par \par \uc2  -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087. \par \par \uc2  -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX \par \par \uc2  -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT \par \par \uc2  -On Bloomberg by entering N