\par\par \b \uc2  MARKETS- \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2      By Wayne Cole \par \uc2 967 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 November 2000\par 04:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      TOKYO, Nov 7 (Reuters) - The euro looked less than stable on \par \par \uc2  Tuesday after two straight sessions of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  achieved \par \par \uc2  little more than keeping it in place. \par \par \uc2      The dollar, meanwhile, held firm on most other major \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the U.S. Presidential election loomed large with \par \par \uc2  the polls still showing the vote too close to call. \par \par \uc2      In late morning trade, the euro was at $0.8615 after easing \par \par \uc2  from an early $0.8638 high, leaving it below where the European \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (ECB) started \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday. \par \par \uc2      It was also under pressure at 92.49 yen having failed to \par \par \uc2  hold Monday's high around 93.60, while the dollar was standing \par \par \uc2  rock steady on the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 107.40 yen. \par \par \uc2      Both the dollar and the yen notched up notable gains on \par \par \uc2  sterling which had been undermined by soft U.K. data on Monday \par \par \uc2  and by a large sterling/yen sell order. The pound was trading \par \par \uc2  down at $1.4285 and 153.50 yen. \par \par \uc2      Not helping the euro was confirmation from Japanese Finance \par \par \uc2  Minister Kiichi Miyazawa that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had not been asked to join \par \par \uc2  in the recent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the ECB. \par \par \uc2      Dealers here have been reluctant to sell euros in case the \par \par \uc2  Bank of Japan stepped into the market, but Miyazawa's comment \par \par \uc2  seemed to lessen that risk. \par \par \uc2      "For the moment anyway the market's assuming that the ECB \par \par \uc2  won't ask for anyone's help because it can't get the States on \par \par \uc2  board this close to the election," said a U.S. bank dealer. \par \par \uc2      "There will be more risk of a full G7 attack after the \par \par \uc2  election, but then again that may change depending on who wins." \par \par \uc2      Traders tend to assume there will be rather less chance of \par \par \uc2  action if Republican contender George W. Bush wins, since his \par \par \uc2  camp criticised the Group of Seven's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in September \par \par \uc2  and is generally viewed as more laissez faire. \par \par \uc2  Thus many thought a Bush victory could lead directly to \par \par \uc2  speculative selling of the euro come Wednesday and a test of \par \par \uc2  support around $0.8555. \par \par \uc2      In any case, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as with everything in markets, is \par \par \uc2  subject to the law of diminishing returns. \par \par \uc2      Traders noted that all three \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  episodes so far \par \par \uc2  had started around the $0.8620/30 level, making that the line in \par \par \uc2  the sand as far as markets were concerned. \par \par \uc2      G7 \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on September 22 had the element of surprise \par \par \uc2  and lifted the euro to $0.9040. \par \par \uc2      But last Friday's lone act by the ECB only reached 88 cents \par \par \uc2  and Monday's effort barely managed a peak of $0.8730 before \par \par \uc2  heavy U.S. fund selling drove the euro lower. \par \par \uc2      BETS ON BUSH \par \par \uc2      As for the election, Democrat Al Gore took a tight 48 to 46 \par \par \uc2  percent lead in Monday's Reuters/MSNBC national tracking poll. \par \par \uc2      But markets were leaning more toward a win by Bush. \par \par \uc2      Betting on the Iowa Electronic Market, which trades future \par \par \uc2  contracts on the election and has an excellent track record of \par \par \uc2  picking past winners, has recently moved heavily in favour of \par \par \uc2  Bush, giving him a 73 percent lead to Gore's 27 percent. \par \par \uc2  Just as importantly, the market is also betting strongly on \par \par \uc2  a clean sweep of the House by the Republicans, an event which \par \par \uc2  would break the policy deadlock of the recent past. \par \par \uc2  Traders reasoned this would not be bullish for the Treasury \par \par \uc2  market which has come to appreciate policy deadlock as a form of \par \par \uc2  forced fiscal discipline. \par \par \uc2  "The risk has to be that with the chains off, these guys \par \par \uc2  (Republicans) are going to spend away the surplus, leaving less \par \par \uc2  and less to buy back bonds," said a European bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  On the other hand, Bush's aggressive tax cuts and \par \par \uc2  pro-business stance was seen as positive for consumer spending \par \par \uc2  and for equities going forward. \par \par \uc2  "On balance, if Wall Street rallies hard the dollar will \par \par \uc2  probably track higher - if only because equities get a lot more \par \par \uc2  media coverage than bonds," added the dealer. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 0251 GMT. All data taken from Reuters \par \par \uc2  with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at 2130 \par \par \uc2  GMT. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab Last     US Close  % Chg  YTD %  1999 Cls\par \tab \tab \tab    06 Nov\par \tab \tab -----------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Euro/dlr   0.8620   0.8611   +0.10   -14.40   1.0070\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Dlr/yen    107.40   107.38   +0.02    +5.08   102.21\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Euro/yen    92.61    92.48   +0.14   -10.17   103.10\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Dlr/swiss  1.7647   1.7666   -0.11   +10.97   1.5902\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Stg/dlr    1.4283   1.4270   +0.09   -11.70   1.6176\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Can/dlr    1.5318   1.5302   +0.10    +5.97   1.4455\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Aus/dlr    0.5266   0.5267   -0.02   -19.76   0.6563\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Euro/swiss 1.5220   1.5213   +0.05    -5.09   1.6036\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Euro/stg   0.6031   0.6030   +0.02    -3.33   0.6239.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bid prices at 0251 GMT. All data taken from Reuters\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at 2130\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par GMT.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab      Last     US Close  % Chg  YTD %  1999 Cls\par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab   06 Nov\par \tab \tab \tab      -----------------------------------------\par  Euro/dlr\tab \tab   0.8620   0.8611   +0.10   -14.40   1.0070\par  Dlr/yen\tab \tab    107.40   107.38   +0.02    +5.08   102.21\par  Euro/yen\tab \tab    92.61    92.48   +0.14   -10.17   103.10\par  Dlr/swiss\tab \tab  1.7647   1.7666   -0.11   +10.97   1.5902\par  Stg/dlr\tab \tab    1.4283   1.4270   +0.09   -11.70   1.6176\par  Can/dlr\tab \tab    1.5318   1.5302   +0.10    +5.97   1.4455\par  Aus/dlr\tab \tab    0.5266   0.5267   -0.02   -19.76   0.6563\par  Euro/swiss\tab \tab 1.5220   1.5213   +0.05    -5.09   1.6036\par  Euro/stg\tab \tab   0.6031   0.6030   +0.02    -3.33   0.6239.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010822dwb702gam\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
