\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  MOF Kuroda - ECB  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  was appropriate. \b0\par\par\uc2 153 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 November 2000\par 01:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Nov 6 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Vice Finance Minister of Inernational Affairs Haruhiko Kuroda said on Monday the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (ECB) acted appropriately when it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Friday to prop up the weak euro. \par \par \uc2  "The euro was too weak against the yen and the dollar. The ECB's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was natural and in line with the G7 (Group of Seven industrial nations) statement in September," Kuroda told reporters. \par \par \uc2  Asked his view on euro movements after the ECB's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Kuroda said: "We need some time to evaluate the impact of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but the ECB's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was an appropriate step." \par \par \uc2  The euro was holding mostly steady in nervous trade in Tokyo on Monday morning, quoted around $0.8650, with the market remaining on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  alert. The euro had spiked as high as 88 cents after Friday's ECB \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010822dwb602oqj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
