\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro boosted by ECB  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2  By Sabrina Ghani \par \uc2 701 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 November 2000\par 12:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Nov 6 (Reuters) - The euro rallied nearly a cent against the dollar on Monday after the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  for a second consecutive trading day to buy the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The ECB said it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  unilaterally and that its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was in line with the statement it had made on Friday when it said its action was prompted by concern about the global and domestic repercussions of the exchange rate of the euro, including its impact on price stability. \par \par \uc2  It also said the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was in line with the statement issued by the Group of Seven industrial nations in September. The ECB's solo forays into the foreign exchanges come about six weeks after the G7 \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  jointly in the euro's support on September 22. \par \par \uc2  But the euro soon began to pare gains, not least because of a batch of weaker-than-expected euro zone data. \par \par \uc2  "When we came in the euro was looking rocky and the ECB \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is exhibiting a degree of success," said Mark Henry, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at GNI. \par \par \uc2  "But as the dust settles, we are struggling to reclaim $0.87 because fundamentals do not justify euro at higher levels. For the sentiment to turnaround we need to see positive euroland economic news. But the data has not been good so far." \par \par \uc2  Monday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  lifted the euro to peaks around $0.8730, before the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  eased back to $0.8670 by 1107 GMT. That leaves it more than a cent below the one-month peaks around $0.88 set after Friday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Traders said the euro's retreat from the day's highs was assisted by euro zone data. \par \par \uc2  Reuters euro zone sevices activity index fell to 57.5, its lowest level since June 1999. Pan-German industry orders fell 4.6 percent in September against a rise of 2.0 percent in August. \par \par \uc2  "The sentiment is still bearish," said Jeremy Hawkins, chief economic adviser at Bank of America in London. \par \par \uc2  "But it (\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) will provide more of a base and shows that Friday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not one-off and they are prepared to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  as frequently as necessary. \par \par \uc2  BOJ WILLING ALLY, BUT U.S. HELP CRUCIAL \par \par \uc2  Traders also said euro zone finance ministers gathering in Brussels for a two-day meeting starting on Monday would likely offer strong verbal support for the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and keep alive wariness of further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the ECB. \par \par \uc2  They added there was also a risk that Japan could help prop up the beleaguered euro, given that gains which the yen has made against the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  have hurt Japanese exporters. \par \par \uc2  Japanese Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs Haruhiko Kuroda said \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would cooperate with the ECB on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  if necessary. \par \par \uc2  However, on a longer-term view, traders said for the euro to convincingly head higher the U.S. would need to join in any action by ECB and BOJ once the U.S. presidential election, on Tuesday, was out of the way. \par \par \uc2  "Unilateral \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  can be effective at the moment and it is helpful that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is willing to support \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  but from the psychological view point, if we want to see a sharp recovery in the euro, the U.S. needs to be involved," said Audrey Childe-Freeman, economist at CIBC World Markets in London. \par \par \uc2  "Only one hour later, it fell to around $0.8680. At the moment the market accepts that the U.S. can't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  but the key is what happens after the elections and if the Republicans come in it is difficult to say they will be as keen as the Democrats to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  Against the yen, the euro rallied to highs around 93.60 yen, up nearly a yen to levels around 93.50, before stabilising below 93 yen. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, comments from MOF's Haruhiko Kuroda earlier curbed the dollar's decline against the yen, pushing it off earlier lows around 107 yen. \par \par \uc2  The dollar dropped to six-week lows below around 106.75 on Friday, triggered by gyrations in euro/yen, which had spiked up and quickly reversed in the wake of the ECB \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010822dwb602o6y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
