\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro rallies after ECB  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2  By Sabrina Ghani \par \uc2 796 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 November 2000\par 14:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Nov 6 (Reuters) - The euro leapt nearly a cent against the dollar on Monday after the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  unilaterally for a second consecutive trading day to buy the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The ECB said that its latest bout of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was in line with its statement on Friday that its action then was prompted by concern about the global and domestic repercussions of the euro's exchange rate, including its impact on price stability. \par \par \uc2  It also said the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was in line with the statement issued by the Group of Seven industrial nations in September. The ECB's solo forays into the foreign exchanges comes about six weeks after the G7 \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  jointly in the euro's support on September 22. \par \par \uc2  But the euro soon pared gains, not least because of a batch of weaker-than-expected data out of the euro zone. \par \par \uc2  "When we came in, the euro was looking rocky and the ECB \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is exhibiting a degree of success," said Mark Henry, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at GNI. \par \par \uc2  "But as the dust settles, we are struggling to reclaim $0.87 because fundamentals do not justify euro at higher levels. For the sentiment to turn around we need to see positive euroland economic news. But the data has not been good so far." \par \par \uc2  Monday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  lifted the euro to peaks around $0.8730, before the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stabilised toward the bottom of the post-\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  range around $0.8660/70 by 1247 GMT. \par \par \uc2  That leaves it more than a cent below the one-month peaks around $0.88 set after Friday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Traders said the euro's retreat from the day's highs was assisted by data showing that the euro zone services activity index fell to 57.5 in October, its lowest since June 1999. Pan-German industry orders fell 4.6 percent in September after a rise of 2.0 percent in August. \par \par \uc2  "The euro has come back down because there are plenty of euro bears and they are not willing to change their view just because of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has not been overwhelming either," said a trader at a Japanese bank in London. \par \par \uc2  "ECB's tactics seem to be to buy small amounts, steadily. However, for now it is enough to limit the downside at around $0.86/$0.8550 because the market knows if they get carried away they will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again, so the risk is more two-way." \par \par \uc2  SENIOR OFFICIALS OFFER EURO, ECB SUPPORT \par \par \uc2  Senior euro zone officials offered verbal support to the euro, keeping alive wariness of further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the ECB. \par \par \uc2  The ECB governing council member and the Bank of Finland governor Matti Vanhala said the ECB was happy with the outcome of its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday and Monday. \par \par \uc2  European Commission President Romano Prodi described the ECB's unilateral market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the euro as a "well calculated risk". \par \par \uc2  Traders expected further verbal support for the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from euro zone finance ministers gathering in Brussels for a two-day meeting starting on Monday. \par \par \uc2  They added there was also a risk that Japan could help prop up the beleaguered euro, given that gains which the yen has made against the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  have hurt Japanese exporters. \par \par \uc2  Japanese Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs Haruhiko Kuroda said \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would cooperate with the ECB on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  if necessary. \par \par \uc2  However, on a longer-term view, traders said if the euro was to head convincingly higher, the United States would need to join in any action by ECB and Japan once Tuesday's U.S. presidential election was out of the way. \par \par \uc2  "Unilateral \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  can be effective at the moment and it is helpful that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is willing to support \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  but from the psychological view point, if we want to see a sharp recovery in the euro, the U.S. needs to be involved," said Audrey Childe-Freeman, economist at CIBC World Markets. \par \par \uc2  "Only one hour later, it fell to around $0.8680. At the moment the market accepts that the U.S. can't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  but the key is what happens after the elections and if the Republicans come in, it is difficult to say they will be as keen as the Democrats to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  The euro rallied to highs around 93.60 yen, up nearly a yen from lows around 92.50, before stabilising below 93 yen. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, comments from MOF's Haruhiko Kuroda earlier curbed the dollar's decline against the yen, pushing it off earlier lows around 107 yen. \par \par \uc2  The dollar dropped to six-week lows below around 106.75 on Friday, triggered by gyrations in euro/yen, which had spiked up and quickly reversed in the wake of the ECB \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010822dwb602n8x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
