\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Recovering euro benefits from dollar's data woes. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Christina Fincher \par \uc2 479 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 November 2000\par 14:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Nov 1 (Reuters) - The euro rose against the dollar for a fifth consecutive day on Wednesday, its longest rally in a year, buoyed by signs of slowing U.S. growth and wariness of euro-supportive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Speculation growth in the euro zone could be overtaking that in the United States sent the euro to two-week highs against the dollar, the yen and the pound. \par \par \uc2  Dealers are awaiting the U.S. NAPM index for October later on Wednesday for further signs the U.S. economy is cooling, following recent weak U.S. data. U.S. third quarter productivity data and employment figures later this week will also be closely watched. \par \par \uc2  "Yesterday's data confirmed that there is a good chance of a fairly aggressive slowdown in the U.S. economy," said Francesca Fornasari, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  economist at Lehman Brothers in London. \par \par \uc2  "There is now a distinct chance that U.S. growth has slipped behind Europe, which is making euro zone assets more attractive in comparison." \par \par \uc2  Lehman Brothers predict euro zone growth of 2.9 percent in the third quarter, just above preliminary U.S. growth estimates for the period of 2.7 percent. \par \par \uc2  The euro stood at $0.8550 at 1250 GMT, over three cents above last week's record lows and just short of earlier highs around $0.8567, according to Reuters data. The euro also rose as high as 92.90 yen , up over four percent from last week's all-time lows around 88.80. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  THREAT IN THIN MARKET \par \par \uc2  Wariness of further euro-buying by central banks was rife after Bundesbank President Ernst Welteke and U.S. Treasury Secretary Lawrence Summers both hinted at \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Thin volumes, due to public holidays in many European countries, were seen providing ideal conditions for further \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action. \par \par \uc2  "The risk of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains, especially at the moment given the euro's mini-uptrend and the fact that turnover is thin, which would exacerbate the move," said Mitul Kotecha, head of global \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  research at Credit Agricole Indosuez in London. \par \par \uc2  Traders said they did not expect the United States to join in any coordinated euro-buying spree just a week before elections, but added there was a good chance the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  may decide to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  by themselves. \par \par \uc2  Sterling, meanwhile, fell to two-week lows beyond 59 pence against the euro after a weaker-than-expected British manufacturing sector survey prompted a downward revision to UK interest rates. \par \par \uc2  The British headline purchasing managers index for October fell below the boom-or-bust 50 level for the first time in 18-months. \par \par \uc2  The Confederation of British Industry, meanwhile, reported its retail sales volume balance for October fell to zero from +14, its worst showing since January, 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010822dwb102xr2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
