\par\par \b \uc2  Fragile euro barely holds above lifetime low. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Chikafumi Hodo \par \uc2 912 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Oktober 2000\par 05:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      TOKYO, Oct 26 (Reuters) - The euro barely held above its \par \par \uc2  lifetime low in Tokyo on Thursday morning, staying fragile after \par \par \uc2  the Group of 20 disappointed the market by failing to come up \par \par \uc2  with a stronger message of support for it. \par \par \uc2      The single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stayed under pressure against the yen and \par \par \uc2  the dollar with speculators eagerly looking for a chance to drive \par \par \uc2  it down towards the psychologically sensitive $0.80 level, \par \par \uc2  dealers said. \par \par \uc2      "The market is looking for all sorts of excuses to sell the \par \par \uc2  euro, and the silence by monetary officials after the G20 meeting \par \par \uc2  has created an excellent excuse to liquidate euro holdings \par \par \uc2  further," a Japanese city dealer said. \par \par \uc2      "Now the market will sell the euro until the market sees \par \par \uc2  another \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said. \par \par \uc2      U.S. Treasury Secretary Lawrence Summers said the G20 meeting \par \par \uc2  informally discussed the euro, but there was no focused \par \par \uc2  discussion on how to support it. \par \par \uc2      More surprisingly, European officials including German \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Hans Eichel, Bank of France Governor Jean-Claude \par \par \uc2  Trichet and European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (ECB) President Wim Duisenberg \par \par \uc2  remained mute on the issue. \par \par \uc2  The market brushed off Bundesbank President Ernst Welteke's \par \par \uc2  standard line that the euro's level does not reflect Europe's \par \par \uc2  economic fundamentals. \par \par \uc2  EYES ON DUISENBERG AND ISSING \par \par \uc2  Japanese officials also commented on the euro on Thursday, \par \par \uc2  but the market's reaction was muted as it doubts \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the euro before the ECB makes a move. \par \par \uc2  Senior Finance Ministry official Zembei Mizoguchi echoed \par \par \uc2  Welteke's remarks, also adding that the ministry "will continue \par \par \uc2  to monitor \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets carefully, always considering \par \par \uc2  the need to take appropriate action." \par \par \uc2  At 0235 GMT, the euro stood at $0.8275/80, near its record \par \par \uc2  low of $0.8246. Against the yen, it was at 89.52/60 yen, also not \par \par \uc2  far off from a record low 88.98 yen. \par \par \uc2  The euro was mostly locked in a tight range in Tokyo as the \par \par \uc2  market is awaiting Duisenberg's speech at 1500 GMT. ECB Chief \par \par \uc2  Economist Otmar Issing is also scheduled to speak on "faith in \par \par \uc2  the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 " from 1600 GMT. \par \par \uc2  JAPANESE INVESTORS \par \par \uc2  Many dealers were wary about possible euro sales by Japanese \par \par \uc2  life insurers and other institutional investors and exporters in \par \par \uc2  the euro/yen cross. \par \par \uc2  Speculation that many life insurers were liquidating their \par \par \uc2  European bond holdings intensified the downward pressure on the \par \par \uc2  euro, although many traders doubt they have started selling on a \par \par \uc2  large scale. \par \par \uc2  "From the daily activity, it's always possible that some \par \par \uc2  insurers are selling European bonds, but if major repatriation \par \par \uc2  had occurred, the euro wouldn't be standing at these levels. It \par \par \uc2  would be much lower," another Japanese bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  "It's true that many insurers liquidated their European \par \par \uc2  assets in September at the end of the mid-term fiscal book \par \par \uc2  closings, but in October many have unwound their hedge positions \par \par \uc2  after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he added. "Many are simply hedging \par \par \uc2  again, reflecting the rapid and unexpected drop of the euro." \par \par \uc2      Dealers said the euro could drop further against the yen as \par \par \uc2  Japanese investors hedge further. \par \par \uc2      Wednesday's fall of the euro in overseas market was also \par \par \uc2  triggered by talk that ING Group NV was selling large amounts of \par \par \uc2  the euro to purchase a U.S. investment bank. The company quickly \par \par \uc2  denied the rumour. \par \par \uc2  The dollar stood near Wednesday's late U.S. level at \par \par \uc2  108.25/30 yen. Dealers said firm bids were placed below 108 yen, \par \par \uc2  while the topside was blocked around 108.50 yen. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the Swiss franc still bearish against the dollar \par \par \uc2  at 1.8201/11 francs after hitting a 14-year low due to the euro's \par \par \uc2  plight. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 0250 GMT. All data taken from Reuters \par \par \uc2  with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at 2130 \par \par \uc2  GMT. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab      Last     US Close  % Chg  YTD %   1999 Cls\par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab   25 Oct.\par \tab \tab \tab      -----------------------------------------\par  Euro/dlr\tab \tab   0.8273   0.8270   +0.04   -17.85   1.0070\par  Dlr/yen\tab \tab    108.31   108.21   +0.09    +5.97   102.21\par  Euro/yen\tab \tab    89.64    89.51   +0.15   -13.06   103.10\par  Dlr/swiss\tab \tab  1.8203   1.8209   -0.03   +14.47   1.5902\par  Stg/dlr\tab \tab    1.4335   1.4316   +0.13   -11.38   1.6176\par  Can/dlr\tab \tab    1.5158   1.5172   -0.09    +4.86   1.4455\par  Aus/dlr\tab \tab    0.5175   0.5198   -0.44   -21.15   0.6563\par  Euro/swiss\tab \tab 1.5061   1.5063   -0.01    -6.08   1.6036\par  Euro/stg\tab \tab   0.5769   0.5772   -0.05    -7.53   0.6239.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bid prices at 0250 GMT. All data taken from Reuters\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at 2130\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par GMT.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab      Last     US Close  % Chg  YTD %   1999 Cls\par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab   25 Oct.\par \tab \tab \tab      -----------------------------------------\par  Euro/dlr\tab \tab   0.8273   0.8270   +0.04   -17.85   1.0070\par  Dlr/yen\tab \tab    108.31   108.21   +0.09    +5.97   102.21\par  Euro/yen\tab \tab    89.64    89.51   +0.15   -13.06   103.10\par  Dlr/swiss\tab \tab  1.8203   1.8209   -0.03   +14.47   1.5902\par  Stg/dlr\tab \tab    1.4335   1.4316   +0.13   -11.38   1.6176\par  Can/dlr\tab \tab    1.5158   1.5172   -0.09    +4.86   1.4455\par  Aus/dlr\tab \tab    0.5175   0.5198   -0.44   -21.15   0.6563\par  Euro/swiss\tab \tab 1.5061   1.5063   -0.01    -6.08   1.6036\par  Euro/stg\tab \tab   0.5769   0.5772   -0.05    -7.53   0.6239.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010822dwaq03f6a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
