\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  View: Dlr Seen Firm But ECB May Create Slick Spots \b0\par\par\uc2  By Christine Richard \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \uc2 602 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Oktober 2000\par 00:01\par \uc2  Emerging Markets Report \par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  NEW YORK -(Dow Jones)- The dollar, having weathered last week's market turmoil with hardly a flinch, is expected to remain strong this week, even as the future of U.S. stocks and the peace process in the Mideast remains far from clear. \par \par \uc2  While \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the euro could come at any time, it is expected to interrupt only briefly the general trend toward a weaker common \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The dollar is seen strong but capped around Y110 against the yen this week, while the euro is seen slipping gradually lower toward 83-82 cents. \par \par \uc2  "There doesn't seem to be any reason to question the almighty dollar," said David Gilmore, a partner at \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  Analytics in Essex, Conn. \par \par \uc2  As euro bulls learned last week, a rebounding U.S. stock market can be a powerful force in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, Gilmore said. \par \par \uc2  The euro spiraled to a new all-time low against the dollar of $0.8324 as investors piled back into U.S. stocks following a sharp selloff early Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  "October has typically been a month for bottoming, and a lot of damage has been done," said David Ethridge, director of capital markets strategy at Standard & Poor's MMS. "Now, people will be looking to see if this bounce has legs." \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Dollar Handles Bad News Well\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Meanwhile, even negative news seems to support the dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Oil prices are definitely creating an unsettled environment for\par stocks," Ethridge said. "But in the past, we have seen that weak stocks\par and volatile stock markets tend to help support the dollar."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Still, the threat of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will overhang the market this week.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The focus will remain on how much more pain the ECB (European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central\par Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ) and the G7 will allow the euro to suffer," Ethridge said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par While dealers are certain to be nervous about the euro testing its\par all-time low, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will reach new lows this week without\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Gilmore said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "It's almost too obvious to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at new lows," he said. "Besides,\par apart from the move on Wednesday, the euro's move down has been\par relatively orderly."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The ECB's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  goal is widely believed to be limited to an\par orderly decline of the single \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rather than long-term stability\par or a rebound.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "I don't think there is \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  coming," said Carl Weinberg,\par chief international economist at High Frequency Economics. "Everything\par we know tells us that they are not playing for levels but for market\par stabilization."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Group of 20 meeting in Montreal at the beginning of the week could\par prove a good opportunity for jawboning the euro higher, even if U.S. and\par euro-zone officials can't agree on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , said Gilmore.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Meanwhile, news reports Friday that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's Kyoei Life Insurance Co.\par will file for court protection could see the yen gain against the\par dollar, Weinberg said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Taking Kyoei and Chiyoda (Mutual Life Insurance, which filed for\par bankruptcy protection earlier this month) together, you have around $70\par billion in assets to be liquidated," said Weinberg. "Even if only 5% or\par around $3.5 billion are foreign assets, you have significant support for\par the yen."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But Ethridge says he expects little reaction, given that failures have\par been expected.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Bankruptcies are part of the cleansing process in Japan's economy,\par and I'd be surprised if it wasn't happening," said Ethridge. "Besides,\par this news wasn't out of the blue."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Christine Richard, Dow Jones Newswires; 201-938-4384;\par christine.richard@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1141 4137 \par \par \uc2 Dokument em00000020010805dwam0049m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
