\par\par \b \uc2  Oil Prices Pose Challenge To Inflation Targeting:Bankers \b0\par\par\uc2 754 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Oktober 2000\par 14:08\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK -(Dow Jones)- Rising oil prices are posing a challenge to inflation-targeting monetary policies as central banks try to prevent the cost of oil from effecting core inflation, Asia-Pacific senior \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials told a seminar Friday. \par \par \uc2  The officials, however, defended the effectiveness of inflation-targeting in controlling \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatility, arguing that targeting could become more flexible but shouldn't necessarily be abandoned under current conditions. \par \par \uc2  "A shock such as oil prices rising, represents a real shock and is a challenge for any \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  not to permit first-round effects entering the system," Murray Sherwin, deputy governor of the Reserve Bank of New Zealand told an inflation-targeting seminar in Bangkok, organized by the Bank of Thailand. \par \par \uc2  He was referring to the danger that high oil prices could feed through to production costs and thereby affect core inflation. \par \par \uc2  Under inflation targeting, a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announces official target ranges for the inflation rate along with an explicit statement that low inflation is the overriding goal of monetary policy. The government generally targets a core inflation rate such as consumer prices excluding volatile food and energy prices. \par \par \uc2  Inflation targeting is one of the policies adopted by some central banks as a means to ensure monetary stability. However, the recent hike in oil prices has threatened inflation targets set by the central banks and at the same time has put pressure on their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The Australian and the New Zealand dollar and the Thai baht have all come under pressure recently. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par         Inflation Targeting Provided "An Anchor"\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Sherwin said that inflation targeting provided "an anchor" to regional\par central banks that no longer pursue a rigid exchange rate regime after\par the 1997 crisis.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  officials said that a return to more rigid exchange\par rate systems would be difficult in the current environment of large and\par volatile capital flows. They said that while \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  remains a\par useful tool to control \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  movements caused by surprise\par shocks such as the high oil prices, it should be used with caution.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  should be used very rarely and with care," said Stephen\par Grenville, deputy governor of the Reserve Bank of Australia.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par He said that a good approach for an inflation-targeting policy during\par volatile periods is that of the Bank of England, which allows inflation\par to deviate from target for a certain period under certain circumstances.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "We need careful specification of the inflation target rather than not\par have a target at all," Grenville said defending his bank's policy.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Chatu Mongol Sonakul, Bank of Thailand governor, said that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's decision to adopt inflation targeting early this year helped push\par yields on the 10-year bond down to 6.1% recently from 7.91% at the\par beginning of the year.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "I'm sure that public confidence in our commitment to control\par inflation was certainly one of the important factors that helped this\par reduction," Chatu Mongol said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Bank of Thailand has set a core inflation target of between zero\par to 3.5% by 2002.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Foreign Exchange Intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Isn't Always Effective\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par On the other hand, Masayuki Matsushima, executive director at the Bank\par of Japan, argued that it could be risky to set a numerical target for\par inflation. While the Bank of Japan has adopted price stability as a\par priority, it has refrained from setting a specific numerical target.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "In view of the current development of prices in Japan, it is\par difficult to set specific numerical values to the definition of price\par stability that are consistent with the sound development of the\par economy," Matsushima said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par He added, however, that the Bank of Japan will explore whether price\par stability can be expressed by "some numerical values" in the future.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Matsushima said that the impact from high oil prices on Japan's and\par other developed economies "was less severe" than in past crises due to\par improved oil conservation policies and a deflationary sentiment in most\par markets.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par He said, however, that some movements in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rate\par can't be overlooked although \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market wasn't always\par effective.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy is still an important and effective tool when\par used at a good timing," Matsushima said. "But just a simple \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market doesn't help to stabilize a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign\par exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  movement," he added, saying that the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has reduced\par its frequency of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Jenny Paris, Dow Jones Newswires; 661-9294817;\par jenny.paris@dowjones.com\par -0- 20/10/00 12-08G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dwak053tw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
