\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro underpinned above post- \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  lows. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Lisa Jucca \par \uc2 631 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Oktober 2000\par 12:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Oct 9 (Reuters) - The euro was in a holding pattern above Friday's post-\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  lows against the dollar and the yen on Monday amid lingering wariness of further joint \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and after a big corporate bankruptcy in \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The failure of Chiyoda Mutual Life Insurance Co, under total debts of some 2.94 trillion yen ($26.95 billion), marked Japan's biggest corporate bankruptcy and spurred renewed doubts about the strength of Japan's recovery. \par \par \uc2  But with Japanese and U.S. markets closed for a holiday on Monday, traders were cautiously waiting to see reactions in financial markets on Tuesday to assess the full impact of the troubled insurer. \par \par \uc2  The thinness of trading volumes was, however, keeping traders on their toes as analysts said an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be more successful if performed in such thin market conditions. \par \par \uc2  "There is some concern the Group of Seven will come in and support the euro," said Ryan Shea, international economist at Bank One in London. \par \par \uc2  "The market is very thin and this sort of situation makes \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  more successful. So it is not the day to go down and try $0.86." \par \par \uc2  "And we've seen another bankruptcy, which suggests Japan's economic situation is still weak. That's why we've seen the yen dropping a little bit," he added. \par \par \uc2  But traders said they expected central bankers to come and rescue the euro only in case of a sharp decline. So far the market had been very quiet. \par \par \uc2  "The possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is still there," said a trader at a European bank in Frankfurt. \par \par \uc2  "The market knows that the ECB can \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but they will only come in when they see uncontrolled moves to the downside. As long as the market stays quietly around $0.87 there's no need for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  By 0945 GMT the euro was hovering around $0.87, more than a third of a cent above $0.8659, Friday's trough since the G7 \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of September 22 according to Reuters data. \par \par \uc2  Against the yen, the euro was holding around 94.75/80, a quarter yen above Friday's late North American trading levels around 94.50 yen. \par \par \uc2  MARKETS MULL LAST WEEK'S ECB RATE HIKE \par \par \uc2  Analysts said dealers were still assessing the implications of last Thursday's quarter percentage point interest rate increase by the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which was making the euro more appealing by narrowing its gap with U.S. rates, but could have an impact on growth. \par \par \uc2  Senior European officials continued to try and soothe the market's fears that the ECB's hike could hurt the euro zone growth in the long run, saying it was justified by fundamentals. \par \par \uc2  The latest of such comments came from ECB Chief Economist Otmar Issing who told a French newspaper the ECB's tightening should bolster public confidence against oil price worries because it ensured \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stability in the longer term. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the U.S. unemployment rate fell to 3.9 percent in September on Friday, confounding forecasts it would stay unchanged from August's 4.1 percent and raising the spectre of more U.S. interest rate rises. \par \par \uc2  The data hurt U.S. stocks, especially the tech-heavy Nasdaq, but bonds benefited from some flight-to-quality buying. \par \par \uc2  By 0950 GMT the dollar was hovering around 109, just below the day's highs and half a yen below last week's seven-week highs around 109.60 yen. \par \par \uc2  "It is a wait-and-see game. It will probably trade the range of 108.70 to 109.25. At about 109.50, there are quite good orders from exporters and also option protection trades," said Karl Broecker, head of treasury at Landesbank Baden-Wuerttemberg. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010822dwa904g9e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
