\par\par \b \uc2  Yen sold after Japan earthquake, euro shaken. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Yoshiko Mori \par \uc2 1,194 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Oktober 2000\par 08:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      TOKYO, Oct 6 (Reuters) - The euro sagged to post-\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  lows in Tokyo on Friday as a surprise rate hike by the European \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (ECB) could not dispel concern over growth in the \par \par \uc2  eurozone. \par \par \uc2      In nervous trade, the euro delved as deep as $0.8671 \par \par \uc2  according to the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ), the lowest since the Group \par \par \uc2  of Seven \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in its defence on September 22. \par \par \uc2      The euro was quoted at $0.8699/8702 at 0525 GMT, compared \par \par \uc2  with $0.8686 in late New York on Thursday. \par \par \uc2      "Speculators are still looking for a good excuse to sell the \par \par \uc2  euro," said Toshihiko Masaki, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at ABN \par \par \uc2  AMRO Bank NV's Tokyo branch. \par \par \uc2      "The ECB could tap the market again (to buy euro) as they are \par \par \uc2  piling up substantial euro short positions." he added. \par \par \uc2      The yen was also under pressure following news an earthquake \par \par \uc2  with a magnitude of 7.1 on the open-ended Richter scale rocked \par \par \uc2  broad areas of western Japan on Friday. \par \par \uc2      Public broadcaster NHK said the quake was powerful enough to \par \par \uc2  knock people off their feet and windows were shattered. \par \par \uc2      The dollar rose to around 108.90 yen soon after news of the \par \par \uc2  earthquake from around 108.70 yen. The dollar kept a firm tone \par \par \uc2  against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 108.89/92 yen at 0525 GMT. \par \par \uc2      The euro had stretched as high as $0.8788 on Thursday after \par \par \uc2  the ECB sprang a surprise 25-basis point rate rise, but the more \par \par \uc2  the market contemplated the move the less it liked it. \par \par \uc2      Rate hikes can sometimes support a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by improving the \par \par \uc2  returns on deposits, but in this case the market was more worried \par \par \uc2  it was overkill for the eurozone economy at a time when many \par \par \uc2  forward indicators were pointing to a slowdown. \par \par \uc2      ECB President Wim Duisenberg claimed the rate rise would \par \par \uc2  support growth, but to no avail. \par \par \uc2      "The ECB view is contradicted by analysts from all quarters \par \par \uc2  (saying) the economy has likely peaked and will slow in the face \par \par \uc2  of higher oil prices, which is a de-facto tightening," Karl \par \par \uc2  Broeker, head of Treasury at Landesbank Baden-Wuerttenberg in \par \par \uc2  Singapore, told Reuters Television. \par \par \uc2  Japan is one of the world's most earthquake prone regions and \par \par \uc2  tens of thousands of tremors have jolted the Izu island chain \par \par \uc2  south of Tokyo in recent months. \par \par \uc2  "Initial market reaction to a big earthquake is always dollar \par \par \uc2  buying for yen, as in the case of today, as it (the tremor) \par \par \uc2  undermines the yen's image," said a city bank trader. \par \par \uc2  But in such a case, the yen is always bought back as the \par \par \uc2  market realises that in a worst-case scenario, Japan - the \par \par \uc2  world's largest creditor nation - would have to liquidate \par \par \uc2  overseas assets, mostly denominated in U.S. dollars and bring \par \par \uc2  money back home to fix damage, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The damage to the yen on Friday was somewhat limited, as the \par \par \uc2  quake hit mostly rural areas of Japan, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had so \par \par \uc2  far failed to gain ground lost after the event. \par \par \uc2  The market was waiting for a September U.S. employment report \par \par \uc2  later on Friday. The jobless rate is seen steady at 4.1 percent, \par \par \uc2  while average hourly earnings should rise a moderate 0.3 percent. \par \par \uc2  The Australian dollar fell to a fresh record trough around \par \par \uc2  $0.5280, partly in sympathy with the weak euro. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 0606 GMT. All data taken from Reuters \par \par \uc2  with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at 2130 \par \par \uc2  GMT. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab Last     US Close  % Chg  YTD %   1999 Cls\par \tab \tab \tab    05 Oct.\par \tab \tab -----------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Euro/dlr   0.8700   0.8686   +0.16   -13.60   1.0070\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Dlr/yen    108.70   109.08   -0.35    +6.35   102.21\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Euro/yen   94.60    94.80   -0.21    -8.24   103.10\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Dlr/swiss  1.7484   1.7508   -0.14    +9.95   1.5902\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Stg/dlr    1.4461   1.4431   +0.21   -10.60   1.6176\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Can/dlr    1.4983   1.4982   +0.01    +3.65   1.4455\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Aus/dlr    0.5320   0.5328   -0.15   -18.94   0.6563\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Euro/swiss 1.5220   1.5221   -0.01    -5.09   1.6036\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Euro/stg   0.6015   0.6016   -0.02    -3.59   0.6239.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The euro had stretched as high as $0.8788 on Thursday after the ECB sprang a surprise 25-basis point rate rise, but the more the market contemplated the move the less it liked it.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Rate hikes can sometimes support a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by improving the returns on deposits, but in this case the market was more worried it was overkill for the eurozone economy at a time when many forward indicators were pointing to a slowdown.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ECB President Wim Duisenberg claimed the rate rise would support growth, but to no avail.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The ECB view is contradicted by analysts from all quarters (saying) the economy has likely peaked and will slow in the face of higher oil prices, which is a de-facto tightening," Karl Broeker, head of Treasury at Landesbank Baden-Wuerttenberg in Singapore, told Reuters Television.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Japan is one of the world's most earthquake prone regions and tens of tremors have jolted the Izu island chain south of Tokyo in recent months.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Initial market reaction to a big earthquake is always dollar buying for yen, as in the case of today, as it (the tremor) undermines the yen's image," said a city bank trader.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In such a case, the yen is always bought back as the market realises that in a worst-case scenario, Japan - the world's largest creditor nation - would have to liquidate overseas assets, mostly denominated in U.S. dollars and bring money back home to fix damage, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The damage to the yen on Friday was somewhat limited, as the quake hit mostly rural areas of Japan, but the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had so far failed to gain ground lost after the event.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The market was waiting for a September U.S. employment report later on Friday. The jobless rate is seen steady at 4.1 percent, while average hourly earnings should rise a moderate 0.3 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Australian dollar fell to a fresh record trough around $0.5280, partly in sympathy with the weak euro.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bid prices at 0606 GMT. All data taken from Reuters\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at 2130\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par GMT.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab      Last     US Close  % Chg  YTD %   1999 Cls\par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab   05 Oct.\par \tab \tab \tab      -----------------------------------------\par  Euro/dlr\tab \tab   0.8700   0.8686   +0.16   -13.60   1.0070\par  Dlr/yen\tab \tab    108.70   109.08   -0.35    +6.35   102.21\par  Euro/yen\tab \tab    94.60    94.80   -0.21    -8.24   103.10\par  Dlr/swiss\tab \tab  1.7484   1.7508   -0.14    +9.95   1.5902\par  Stg/dlr\tab \tab    1.4461   1.4431   +0.21   -10.60   1.6176\par  Can/dlr\tab \tab    1.4983   1.4982   +0.01    +3.65   1.4455\par  Aus/dlr\tab \tab    0.5320   0.5328   -0.15   -18.94   0.6563\par  Euro/swiss\tab \tab 1.5220   1.5221   -0.01    -5.09   1.6036\par  Euro/stg\tab \tab   0.6015   0.6016   -0.02    -3.59   0.6239.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dwa605e7j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
