\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  share of euro  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  seen at $1.3 bln. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Masayuki Kitano \par \uc2 561 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Oktober 2000\par 08:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Oct 6 (Reuters) - The latest data on Japan's foreign reserves supports market estimates that Japan spent $1.3 billion as part of joint Group of Seven \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  last month to support the beleagured euro, analysts said on Friday. \par \par \uc2  "Deposits parked with foreign central banks and the Bank for International Settlements rose by $1.307 billion, which probably reflects the amount of the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's euro-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Sayuri Kawamura, senior economist for the \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  Research Institute. \par \par \uc2  Earlier the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) said Japan's foreign reserves rose to $348.948 billion at the end of September, up $4.088 billion from the end of August. \par \par \uc2  "The rise in foreign reserves at the end of September includes the impact from the joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  conducted on September 22," a \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) official confirmed. \par \par \uc2  But the MOF official declined to comment on how much of the $4.1 billion increase was directly caused by the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "Our policy is to release \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  amounts every quarter, and the data for the July-September quarter will be released in November," the MOF official said. \par \par \uc2  The G-7 nations jointly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on September 22 after the euro fell to a record low of $0.8465 on September 20, down nearly 28 percent since its launch. \par \par \uc2  Europe, Japan and the United States were believed to have spent the most to buck up the hapless euro, while Britain and Canada spent smaller amounts. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the rise in Japan's foreign reserves in September was consistent with earlier market estimates placing the amount of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's euro-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at around $1.3 billion or 1.5 billion euros and total \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the G7 at $5-6 billion. \par \par \uc2  The European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is estimated to have spent three to five billion euros (around $2.5 billion to $4.5 billion), and the United States $1.3 billion. \par \par \uc2  MOF's foreign reserve data also contained the amount of a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap transaction conducted between the Bank of Japan and the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (ECB), which analysts think was done to fund ECB buying of the euro with yen. \par \par \uc2  "The ECB probably borrowed yen from the BOJ so that it could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in euros against yen on its own," said CSFB's Tanaka. \par \par \uc2  "The swap transaction suggests that the ECB may have conducted about half of its euro-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , now estimated at around 3 billion euros, against the yen and half in dollars," Tanaka said. \par \par \uc2  The MOF's foreign reserves data showed a $1.324 billion rise in short positions in forwards and futures in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  vis-a-vis the yen. \par \par \uc2  "This data reflects a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap transaction conducted between the BOJ and ECB," said another MOF official, who declined to comment on specifics such as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  involved. \par \par \uc2  The ECB has confirmed that it has conducted a swap transaction with the BOJ in the week ending on September 29. \par \par \uc2  MOF's data shows that the $4.088 billion rise in Japan's foreign reserves in September was mainly due to a $1.694 billion rise in holdings of foreign securities and a $2.526 billion rise in deposits, of which $1.307 billion were deposited at foreign central banks and the Bank for International Settlements (BIS). \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dwa6059xm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
