\par\par \b \uc2  Japan Sep Foreign Reserves $348.94 Billion; + $4.08 Billion On Mo \b0\par\par\uc2 257 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Oktober 2000\par 01:51\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- Japan's reserves of convertible foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , gold and International Monetary Fund special drawing rights in September were up $4.08 billion from the preceding month to $348.9 billion, the finance ministry said Friday. \par \par \uc2  The increase was mainly the result of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets on Sept. 22 when \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  participated in a coordinated effort by major central banks led by the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the ailing euro. The finance ministry is expected to release the data on its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  carried out during the July-September quarter in early November. \par \par \uc2  After a decline of $28.0 million in August, the increase in September left Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves at record levels and the highest in the world, judging from most recent statistics available in each country. Following Japan was the euro-zone with $265.7 billion at the end of July. \par \par \uc2  Briefing reporters on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market's developments over the last month, a senior finance ministry official said the yen's strongest level in September was Y108.14 to the dollar, posted Sept. 25, and the yen's weakest level came on Sept. 8 at Y105.07 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  -By Hidenobu Kageyama, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; hidenobu.kageyama@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  (