\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen relieved at tankan, but dollar still dominant. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Wayne Cole \par \uc2 841 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Oktober 2000\par 04:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Oct 3 (Reuters) - The yen recouped a little lost ground on Tuesday after a generally upbeat Japan "tankan" business survey confounded dark rumours of a weak result. \par \par \uc2  The euro was still nursing losses suffered after a key eurozone business indicator on Monday showed its fifth straight monthly fall, suggesting slowing growth there. \par \par \uc2  Japan's closely-watched sentiment indicator for large manufacturers hit a three year high at plus 10 in the October survey, some way above median market forecasts of plus seven. \par \par \uc2  The result caught the market long of dollars, since many had bought in New York on rumours the survey would be weaker than expected, and prompted a brief selloff. \par \par \uc2  But the dollar dipped only slightly to 108.60 yen in late morning trade from 108.75 just ahead of the data, having scored a six-week high around 108.98 through brokers on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers reported solid support for the dollar at 108.40 and 108.05 and a general expectation for further gains to test the top of a major triangle formation around 109.10 which has lasted since February. \par \par \uc2  Neither was the yen helped by news Thomson Financial BankWatch had downgraded its sovereign risk rating outlook for Japan to negative from stable. \par \par \uc2  The move follows Moody's decision in September to actually cut Japan's domestic rating a notch to Aa2. \par \par \uc2  And traders reported much talk of Japanese investors shifting funds abroad in the search for better returns now that the new fiscal half year had started. Combined with signs that foreign investors were lightening their weighting in Tokyo equities, it was tending to depress the yen on a range of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  However, the euro had failed to benefit much since a key eurozone indicator of business activity released on Monday had shown a fifth consecutive monthly fall in September. \par \par \uc2  That kept the euro at 95.25 yen from 95.23 in New York and a high near 96.00 on Monday. \par \par \uc2  The single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also under pressure from the dollar at $0.8772 having shed around three quarters of a cent on Monday. Traders said the market was itching to sell the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but remained too wary of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to threaten major support around 87 cents. \par \par \uc2  As for \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's tankan, analysts noted that it perfectly illustrated the dichotomy between the country's super efficient exporters and the hidebound domestic-oriented industries. \par \par \uc2  Large manufacturers for instance revised up their investment plans, expecting to spend a hefty 13.8 percent more in fiscal year 2000, so that capital spending for all large firms was estimated to increase by 6.0 percent. \par \par \uc2  Non-manufacturers and small firms lagged badly, reflecting the subdued state of domestic demand, though there were signs that the strength seen in the top firms was trickling down. \par \par \uc2  Both medium-and small-sized manufacturers were planning to spend between five and 10 percent more on investment. \par \par \uc2  "Medium-sized businesses are often overlooked, but the manufacturing sector here showed a sharp upward revision to capex forecasts and that has to be promising," said James Malcolm, an economist at J.P. Morgan. \par \par \uc2  "So overall, it shows the recovery is continuing and there's little evidence in this survey that it's in any danger, which may be a surprise to some given the rise in oil prices." \par \par \uc2  Japan imports all its oil and the steady climb in prices to above $30 a barrel has imposed extra costs on industry. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the market was awaiting the outcome of no less than four \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy meetings in Australia, the United States, United Kingdom and the eurozone. \par \par \uc2  Of these, the Reserve Bank of Australia was considered by analysts as the most likely to hike rates with a Reuters poll putting the chance of a move at 70 percent. \par \par \uc2  But none of 29 primary dealers polled expected the Federal Reserve to tighten at its meeting on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's board meeting on Thursday was considered a closer affair, though on balance analysts expected the bank to wait until later in the month before tightening. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 0206 GMT. All data taken from Reuters \par \par \uc2  with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at 2130 \par \par \uc2  GMT. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab      Last     US Close  % Chg  YTD %   1999 Cls\par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab   02 Oct.\par \tab \tab \tab      -----------------------------------------\par  Euro/dlr\tab \tab   0.8774   0.8770   +0.05   -12.87   1.0070\par  Dlr/yen\tab \tab    108.65   108.80   -0.14    +6.30   102.21\par  Euro/yen\tab \tab    95.18    95.23   -0.05    -7.68   103.10\par  Dlr/swiss\tab \tab  1.7348   1.7363   -0.09    +9.09   1.5902\par  Stg/dlr\tab \tab    1.4661   1.4660   +0.01    -9.37   1.6176\par  Can/dlr\tab \tab    1.5092   1.5091   +0.01    +4.41   1.4455\par  Aus/dlr\tab \tab    0.5431   0.5459   -0.51   -17.25   0.6563\par  Euro/swiss\tab \tab 1.5225   1.5230   -0.03    -5.06   1.6036\par  Euro/stg\tab \tab   0.5978   0.5980   -0.03    -4.18   0.6239.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dwa305pen\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\