\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  Options-Dlr/yen vols languish in shadow of euro. \b0\par\par\uc2 385 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 September 2000\par 23:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  CHICAGO, Sept 26 (Reuters) - Implied volatility in one-month dollar/yen options nestled near a multiyear low on Tuesday as the threat of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the euro continued to grab the market's attention. \par \par \uc2  Volatility in one-month options was quoted at a mid of 9.50 percent, near recent lows, as dollar/yen stayed tethered near 107.50 spot on the day. However, pushing much below current levels may be difficult, traders said. \par \par \uc2  "The front end is pretty low, very close to historics. It will be tough to find sellers at this juncture," one \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  options trader said. "After \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday, I think people are very nervous in general." \par \par \uc2  The United States, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Britain, Canada and the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday to push the euro higher. The possibility of more \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued to prop the euro early this week with the market focused on a referendum on Thursday to determine whether Denmark adopts the euro. \par \par \uc2  "The market is generally long dollar/yen waiting for some kind of big movement either way, but it is a tough position to have because dollar/yen hasn't really moved anywhere so that is eating up a lot of time decay," he said. \par \par \uc2  The options rely on a spot movement either way and that might come in dollar/yen through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in euro/yen, traders said. The 9.00 percent area should prove supportive in one-month dollar/yen options otherwise, they added. \par \par \uc2  Euro/yen one-month volatility was quoted near 16.50 percent on Tuesday afternoon, which was down from about 17.50 percent on Friday morning after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The spread in implied volatility between dollar/yen and euro/dollar one-month options has widened to a steep six percentage points plus favouring the euro, the widest it has ever been on the euro side. The spread had favoured dollar/yen by a wide margin in the spring. \par \par \uc2  The euro/dollar vol near 15.50 percent appears warranted and yen vol is trading very close to fair value, traders said. \par \par \uc2  "Until the spot makes up its mind and moves one way or the other, people are just sitting on the sidelines and worrying more about their euro and cable exposure," he said. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw9q06gbp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
