\par\par \b \uc2  Japan MOF Mutoh: Will Take Steps In  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  Market If Needed \b0\par\par\uc2 264 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 September 2000\par 10:12\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- The top bureaucrat at Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Monday that Japan will take appropriate steps as the need arises with regard to foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  Speaking at his first official press conference since Japan joined the U.S., the E.U. and others in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets in support of the euro Friday, Administrative Vice Finance Minister Toshiro Mutoh, said "Japan will continue to closely monitor the situation and take appropriate steps in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets if necessary." \par \par \uc2  Mutoh responded to a question asking whether \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would follow up on its actions Friday and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again. \par \par \uc2  Mutoh declined to discuss the amount the government used in the market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Asked about his thoughts on the Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market's reaction Monday to the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Mutoh noted that exchange rates were largely in line with their levels after the coordinated action. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was last weekend and the market has maintained (the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  level). In that sense, the Group of Seven was able to make its concern clear to the market," Mutoh said. \par \par \uc2  Monday was the first the first full day Tokyo financial markets were open after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Late Monday in Tokyo, the euro was at $0.8780, higher than $0.8604 the same time Friday. Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y94.62 compared to the levels around Y92.00 Friday in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Audrey McAvoy, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929;\par audrey.mcavoy@dowjones.com\par -0- 25/09/00 09-08G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw9p04n1u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
