\par\par \b \uc2  Japan's Miyazawa says joint  \highlight22\uc2 fx \highlight\uc2  action had impact. \b0\par\par\uc2 457 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 September 2000\par 15:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  PRAGUE, Sept 23 (Reuters) - Japanese Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa said on Saturday Friday's joint \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had an impact on the markets, and the Group of Seven (G7) nations would discuss the euro's situation further at their meeting this afternoon, a finance ministry official said. \par \par \uc2  Miyazawa met with his German and American counterparts prior to the meeting of G7 finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governors on Saturday. \par \par \uc2  Earlier, Miyazawa indicated he was grateful that the European and U.S. authorities had decided to step in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to help the ailing European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "It was good of them to make a decision at the weekend," he told reporters on his way to the G7 meeting. \par \par \uc2  German Finance Minister Hans Eichel expressed gratitude that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had participated in joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the official said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  - the first joint \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action involving the U.S. Federal Reserve, the Bank of Japan and European central banks since 1995 - drove the euro up sharply to above $0.90, although the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  later gave up some of these gains. \par \par \uc2  On rising oil prices, German Finance Minister Hans Eichel told Miyazawa that rising oil prices would be on the agenda of the G7 meeting, but they did not discuss it further, the MOF official said. \par \par \uc2  Separately, Summers explained President Bill Clinton's decision on Friday to order an emergency release from the Strategic Petroleum Reserve for only the second time in history. \par \par \uc2  On macroeconomic policy, Miyazawa told his counterparts that Japan will continue to take stimulative measures to support Japan's gradual economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  Last week, Japan decided on Wednesday on a fresh spending package of a relatively modest 3.5 trillion yen ($33 billion) to 4.0 trillion yen to ensure the economy maintains its course toward recovery. \par \par \uc2  Miyazawa said the government would try to curb Japanese government bond issuances as much as possible in financing the budget. \par \par \uc2  The government is planning to submit the budget to parliament in November. \par \par \uc2  Bank of Japan Governor Masaru Hayami, who also attended the bilateral meeting with the United States, said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue to maintain an accommodative monetary stance to support the economy even after it abandoned its 18-month zero interest rate policy. \par \par \uc2  It was the first credit tightening by Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a decade. \par \par \uc2  Neither Summers nor U.S. Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan, who also attended the meeting, commented on Japan's economy or monetary policy, the official said. \par \par \uc2  Miyazawa also separately met with the Indonesian chief economics Minister Fizal Ramli. \par \par \uc2  Miyazawa pledged to continue supporting Indonesia, but that the nation would have to make more effort on the conflict going on in East Timor. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw9n06ll2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
