\par\par \b \uc2  ECB  \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention \highlight\uc2  - how it works. \b0\par\par\uc2 725 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 September 2000\par 20:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      In FRANKFURT story headlined "ECB \b \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  - how \par \par \uc2   it works" please read in para two ...Europe's first joint \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since 1995... instead of ....the first \par \par \uc2   joint \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action since 1995... \par \par \uc2  (A corrected repetition follows) \par \par \uc2  FRANKFURT, Sept 22 (Reuters) - The European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets for the first time, but kept the market guessing about how it executed the joint action with the U.S. Federal Reserve and Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Europe's first joint \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action since 1995, drove the battered euro up sharply, although the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gave up some of these gains as financial markets fought back. \par \par \uc2  The ECB, which launched the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in January 1999, said the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had taken place following concern about the potential implications of recent moves in the euro, which tumbled to record lows this week. \par \par \uc2  While the ECB gave no details of the \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it is clear that it chose a high-calibre concerted action involving its counterparts representing the two other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  blocs and other central banks within and outside the euro area. \par \par \uc2  ECB President Wim Duisenberg, speaking at the European Parliament on September 12, said that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would consult with other big players in the market - U.S. and Japanese authorities - before acting. \par \par \uc2  More than consulting, he enlisted their help, along with that of Germany's Bundesbank, the Bank of France, the Bank of Canada, the British Treasury and probably several others. \par \par \uc2  THE PROCEDURE \par \par \uc2  While a full-scale concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  carried out jointly with the United States and \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been long seen as the most viable option for the young \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the ECB had - and still has - a choice of options. \par \par \uc2  * Co-ordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  involving only a selected number of national central banks, and possibly key partners from outside of the euro area, probably the option chosen. \par \par \uc2  * High profile \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  involving all 11 national central banks of the euro area. This would allow the ECB to maximise the impact by springing a surprise on markets and including as many market participants as possible. \par \par \uc2  * \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by 11 euro area banks but according to individual timeframes and quotas. \par \par \uc2  * Unilateral \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the ECB alone. \par \par \uc2  POOLED RESOURCES \par \par \uc2  The ECB said in its January monthly report that both in the case of the unilateral and concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves involved would be those pooled at the ECB. \par \par \uc2  Depending on the course of action, the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be either carried out directly by the ECB and/or by national central banks acting on its behalf on a disclosed agency basis. This means that the banks would use ECB reserves and notify their partners in the financial markets that the \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  was carried out for the ECB. \par \par \uc2  The ECB also stressed that, if need be, it could fund \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  through other means than its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, such as \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps, including swaps with other central banks. \par \par \uc2  "Should the need arise, the capacity of the ECB to carry out \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not, therefore, restricted to foreign reserve holdings," the ECB said. \par \par \uc2  The ECB probably informed politicians ahead of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  but they would not have been part of the actual decision-making. \par \par \uc2  The ECB's governing council discussed and prepared the move, if necessary via a phone conference before the decision by the ECB board. \par \par \uc2  INSTITUTIONAL FRAMEWORK \par \par \uc2  Article 107 of the Maastricht Treaty lists \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  among "basic tasks" of the ECB and 11 national central banks making up the so-called Eurosystem. \par \par \uc2  Those \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  must be carried out in accordance with Article 111 of the Treaty, which allows European Union finance ministers, the so called Ecofin council, to create "without prejudice to price stability" institutional frameworks for the relations of the euro exchange rate against other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  One option envisages the Ecofin council concluding formal agreements on an exchange rate system for the euro against other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as U.S. dollar or the Japanese yen. \par \par \uc2  The second option allows the council to draw up "general orientations for exchange-rate policy." \par \par \uc2  But so far neither of the two procedures has been used. \par \par \uc2  Finance ministers and central bankers agreed in December 1997 that ministers would not regularly set targets to guide markets and would attempt to influence \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates in "exceptional circumstances" only. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw9m06rt4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
