\par\par \b \uc2  Comments from policymakers on  \highlight22\uc2 fx intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 529 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 September 2000\par 16:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Sept 22 (Reuters) - Here are quotes from leading politicians and policymakers following joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by major industrial powers in support of the euro on Friday: \par \par \uc2  EUROPEAN UNION - European Economic Affairs Commissioner Pedro Solbes welcomed European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 -led \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  saying it lent credibility to verbal warnings issued about the exchange rate. "It's a good decision," Solbes was quoted by his spokesman as saying. "It demonstrates that when ministers, the Commission and the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  have jointly expressed their concern (about the exchange rate) they really meant it," Solbes said. It also demonstrated that economic policy coordination was working well, he added. \par \par \uc2  DENMARK - Asked if ECB \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of the euro would affect Denmark's referendum on whether to join, Danis Prime Minister Poul Nyrup Rasmussen said "No, I don't think so," at a news conference. "I would not say that that would have any big role to play," said Rasmussen, an active pro-euro campaigner. "We have passed that period where the euro's exchange rate plays a dominant role in people's mind," he said. \par \par \uc2  FRANCE - French Finance Minister Laurent Fabius said he fully backed a concerted round of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . "As president of the Eurogroup, I have been informed by Wim Duisenberg, the president of the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , of the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 ...and I fully approve it," the statement concluded. \par \par \uc2  GERMANY - Germany's Finance Ministry said it welcomed the concerted move to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  following concern about euro weakness. "We are glad about this current development," a spokesman said of the move. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Hans Eichel, asked about the move at a news conference on a separate matter, declined to comment but said he would welcome a rise in the European single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  BRITAIN - A British Treasury spokesman said "As a member of the G7, we share a concern about the potential implications on recent movements is the level of the euro for the world economy," he said. "We believe \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is only effective if public and concerted, as this was." \par \par \uc2  ITALY - Italian Treasury Minister Vincenzo Visco said "The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  puts into action the decisions taken by EU finance ministers in Versailles, and subsequently supported by the (bank) governors, to strengthen the euro in the interests of Europe," Visco said in a statement. "Italy's interests are obviously the same. Therefore, from Italy there is full support for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the first effects of which appear to confirm its effectiveness," Visco added. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 JAPAN\b0 \highlight\uc2  - Japanese Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa said the decision to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  was probably linked to rising oil prices. \par \par \uc2  NETHERLANDS - The Dutch Finance Ministry said it welcomed the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . "We knew about it, we're happy with it, but it's an ECB (European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) matter so that's all I'm going to say," a spokesman told Reuters \par \par \uc2  SWEDEN - Sweden's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Riksbank, said it would not comment on whether it took part in the concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . "We have no comment. We don't comment whether we have or we haven't or whether anyone else has or has not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Riksbank spokesman Thomas Lundberg told Reuters. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw9m06jck\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
