\par\par \b \uc2  Fed's Ferguson Declines Comment On  \highlight22\uc2 Forex Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 143 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 September 2000\par 16:08\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  WASHINGTON -(Dow Jones)- Federal Reserve Vice Chairman Roger Ferguson declined to comment Friday on joint international \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the embattled euro \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The Federal Reserve and the Treasury have a nice division of labor when it comes to discussing \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, and that division basically is that the Treasury talks about \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, so I won't have any response to your question," Ferguson told reporters after an appearance at a Treasury-sponsored conference on electronic financial transactions. \par \par \uc2  Earlier Friday morning, the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Fed and the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  - at the ECB's invitation - \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of the euro. Treasury Secretary Lawrence Summers is scheduled to hold a briefing this morning on the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  -By Jonathan Nicholson, Dow Jones Newswires; 202-862-9255; jonathan.nicholson@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010804dw9m00o7o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
