\par\par \b \uc2  US Treasury Confirms Joint  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  To Buy Euro \b0\par\par\uc2 409 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 September 2000\par 13:22\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  WASHINGTON -(Dow Jones)- The U.S. Treasury Department confirmed Friday that it combined with the monetary authorities of Europe and \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to buy the euro - marking the first time concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been used to back the euro since its launch in January 1999. \par \par \uc2  Around 1145 GMT, the euro was trading at $0.8900, up from $0.8585 at 0700 GMT. \par \par \uc2  A U.S. Treasury Department spokesperson, in a telephone interview, confirmed the joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the Federal Reserve, the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "At the invitation of the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the monetary authorities of the U.S. and \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  joined with the ECB in a concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in exchange markets because of their shared concern about the potential implications of recent movements in the euro for the world economy," the spokesperson said. \par \par \uc2  Speculation about a joint move in favor of the euro had been growing in recent days because of the euro's continuing decline. But few in the markets anticipated such an action only a day before finance ministers and central bankers from the Group of Seven major industrialized nations are due to meet in Prague. \par \par \uc2  A Treasury official said the U.S. used "our own money" to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in support of the euro.  The official confirmed that while the Fed acted at the "invitation" of the ECB, it wasn't acting as an agent for the ECB. On occasion, the Fed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets as an agent for other countries, using their funds to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the U.S. market. \par \par \uc2  In an effort to assert that the initiative came from the ECB, the central banks of Japan and the U.S. didn't begin their euro purchases until after the ECB entered the market. The Fed sold dollars for euros, and the Bank of Japan sold yen for euros. \par \par \uc2  U.S. Treasury Secretary Lawrence Summers is expected to shed further light on the joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  during a media briefing scheduled for 10:00 A.M. EDT (1400 GMT) at the Treasury Department. The briefing originally was scheduled to provide Summers an opportunity to discuss his plans for the G7 meetings in Prague, held are on the sidelines of the joint annual meetings of the International Monetary Fund and the World Bank. \par \par \uc2  -By Damian Milverton, Dow Jones Newswires; 202-862-9272; damian.milverton@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010804dw9m00o5v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
