\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro treads water above record lows, wary of G7. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Deepthi Wickremasinghe \par \uc2 830 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 September 2000\par 14:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Sept 21 (Reuters) - The euro hovered above the previous day's record lows against the dollar and the yen on Thursday as it sought support from the Group of Seven finance ministers' meeting this weekend to save it from new lows. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said ongoing negative sentiment towards the euro and the economies of the euro zone was balanced only by wariness about what the G7 finance ministers might come up with when they meet in Prague on Saturday. \par \par \uc2  "The focus really is on G7 and if we see any strong comment with regard to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  risks for the euro," said Mitul Kotecha, head of global \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  research at Credit Agricole Indosuez. \par \par \uc2  "We are in an environment where the misalignment between major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  is at a significant extreme level so the implication is that the G7 may perhaps do more than they have at past meetings." \par \par \uc2  The euro was trading at 90.44/54 by 1145 GMT according to Reuters data, within half a yen from record lows set on Wednesday. It had retreated from a brief foray above 91 yen earlier in the day. \par \par \uc2  Against the dollar, the euro had eased around half a cent from a peak of $0.8550 according to Reuters data, and was within one cent of Wednesday's record troughs. \par \par \uc2  Traders said interest to buy euros earlier had been fuelled by talk that the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (ECB) was again buying the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as part of its previously announced sales of interest income earned on its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves. \par \par \uc2  Purchases of euros were said to have been in yen and dollars whereas in recent days they had just been in dollars. \par \par \uc2  While traders deemed it prudent to square positions ahead of the G7 meeting in Prague on Saturday, there was scepticism that the finance ministers would come up with a convincing rescue package for the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "We do expect them to say something about the euro but nothing dramatic, but even so it is normal for short term accounts to close their positions so we are getting a squeeze higher," said Jesper Dannesboe, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Dresdner Kleinwort Benson in London. \par \par \uc2  "The bias for now should be to wait for rallies and then sell the rallies on a view that nothing major will come out of the G7." \par \par \uc2  ECB NOT EXPECTED TO ACT ALONE \par \par \uc2  Japanese financial daily Nihon Keizai Shimbun reported on Thursday that the ECB may have started considering solo \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the euro's slump. \par \par \uc2  The report quoted ECB sources as saying it was unrealistic to persist with the option of tripartite \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  with the United States, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Europe. \par \par \uc2  But the report also said it was unclear whether the ECB would conduct unilateral \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy euros as there were concerns within the ECB that such action would have only a limited effect. \par \par \uc2  The market shrugged off the report as the sourcing was vague. \par \par \uc2  "One of the main drivers of euro weakness is still portfolio flows," said Dannesboe at Dresdner. \par \par \uc2  "If they \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  now the signal they are sending to the market is that they aim to slow the decline. They can't really trigger a trend reversal because there is no speculative bubble to burst." \par \par \uc2  U.S. Treasury Secretary Lawrence Summers underlined Washington's reluctance to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  late on Wednesday by reiterating support for the U.S. "strong dollar" policy. \par \par \uc2  But Summers also said he was "closely watching" world \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and energy markets, leaving the possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  open, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "Everyone is looking to see if the U.S. comes a little bit stronger towards an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  move," said Kotecha at Credit Agricole Indosuez. \par \par \uc2  OIL IN SPOTLIGHT \par \par \uc2  The main focus for G7 was expected to be oil prices. \par \par \uc2  U.S. Democratic presidential candidate Al Gore on Thursday called on President Bill Clinton to release oil from the nations Strategic Petroleum Reserves to help stabilise high oil prices. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the psychological impact of that could lead to some dampening on oil prices which might in turn lead to some curbing of dollar strength. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar has to some extent been moving hand-in-hand with oil prices," said Kotecha. \par \par \uc2  News of slower-than-expected economic activity in Japan in July briefly propped up the dollar against the yen, but it has since drifted off to one-week lows around 106.33 according to Reuters data. \par \par \uc2  Economic activity in Japan slowed 1.0 percent in July from the previous month, the Ministry of International Trade and Industry's (MITI) all-industries index showed on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  A core component of the all-industries index, the tertiary sector, mainly comprising service industries, fell 1.1 percent. \par \par \uc2  These indices are seen as useful pointers to gross domestic product data, suggesting that the third quarter got off to a soft start, though analysts remain reasonably confident of a bounce back in August and September. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw9l06u9i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
