\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  Asia: Markets Brace For Weak Euro, Rising Oil Prices \b0\par\par\uc2  By Ron Harui \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \uc2 834 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 September 2000\par 07:30\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets are bracing for further declines in the euro amid widespread notions that finance officials from the Group of Seven industrialized nations won't come up with anything more than a tepid warning about the perils of its weakness. \par \par \uc2  The main beneficiary in the market will be the yen, some analysts say. \par \par \uc2  Finance ministers and central bankers from the G7 are scheduled to gather in Prague this weekend ahead of International Monetary Fund and World Bank meetings. In the past, G7 officials have used such occasions to signal distress about overshot \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Hints about coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  have sometimes been able to stymie a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  move that has strayed too far from economic fundamentals. \par \par \uc2  But this time around, nothing of that sort is likely to emerge, according to a fund manager at a Japanese asset management firm. \par \par \uc2  "\b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market players are hoping that this weekend's G7 meeting will provide a strong stimulus to the euro, but I think they'll be disappointed," he said, adding, "I believe you could see a sell-off in most cross-yen \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  either before or after the G7 meeting, depending on the timing of sales from overseas speculators." \par \par \uc2  Against the yen, the euro could fall as low as Y88.60, while the dollar could well drop to Y105.50 and the sterling pound decline to Y145 within the next one to two weeks, he said. \par \par \uc2  At 0300 GMT, the euro was quoted at Y91.46, the dollar was at Y107.14 and the sterling pound was at Y149.76. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    G7 Communique On Falling Euro, Rising Oil Prices Likely\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Given the prolonged decline of the euro recently, the G7 officials are\par likely to issue a communique at the conclusion of their meeting that\par includes a pledge to watch \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets closely. The\par officials are also likely to promise appropriate action to curb sharp\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  moves as needed, analysts said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "I think the G7 meeting will come out with a carefully worded\par communique that says the G7 nations are monitoring the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets\par closely and will take proper steps against the markets overshooting,"\par the fund manager said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The key question for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  players about any G7 action, however, is\par whether the G7 communique contains any concrete reference to coordinated\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to support the euro. Most analysts say this is highly\par unlikely because some European officials - most notably German\par Chancellor Gerhard Schroeder - have indicated recently that they aren't\par all that concerned about the weak euro, as it benefits the region's\par exporters.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Meantime, U.S. policymakers aren't likely to agree to sell dollars\par because the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is already at relatively weak levels against\par the yen and the U.S. needs, if anything, to ensure dollar stability in\par order to keep foreign investors confident about U.S. investments.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The major question is whether the G7 nations reach an agreement on\par joint \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . At this time we don't expect this to happen as the\par U.S. won't participate in any such action as it needs a strong dollar to\par finance its current account deficit," said Marshall Gittler, senior\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at Bank of America in Tokyo.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par While \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  probably would be willing to participate in coordinated\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to prop up the euro against the yen, doubts linger over\par whether the European monetary authorities will ask for help from Japan,\par analysts said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "I heard that the Japanese monetary authorities were criticized by the\par European monetary authorities as they had \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the euro/yen\par earlier this year without their approval, so \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will need the green\par light from Europe before \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (in euro/yen) again," Gittler said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa voiced the Japan stance on the euro\par last week, when he grumbled about the mixed messages coming out of\par Europe regarding the common \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The G7 meeting is also expected to discuss rising oil prices and\par address this in its communique, but any spillover benefits for the euro\par and other \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  should be limited, analysts said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The recent rise in oil prices globally is a problem (for the G7),\par especially in Europe due to the widespread protests against rising\par energy costs there," said Ryohei Muramatsu, treasury and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign\par exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  manager at Commerzbank.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par While the G7 might express concerns about rising oil prices, notions\par that the G7 nations are somewhat powerless to act against these price\par increases could spark worries about rising inflation in Europe and, by\par extension, a possible hike in interest rates by the European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central\par Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "If inflation increases in Europe because of rising energy costs, the\par ECB could hike interest rates further. This could stifle the euro-zone's\par economic growth and weigh on the euro \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," Muramatsu said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par During the next one week, Muramatsu forecasts the euro could weaken to\par as low as Y90.00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Ron Harui, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929;\par ron.harui@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  4258 5095 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw9i04i64\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
