\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen deflated by downgrade, pound roundly beaten. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Sabrina Ghani \par \uc2 731 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 September 2000\par 14:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Sept 8 (Reuters) - The yen fell against the dollar and the euro on Friday after a downgrade of Japan's sovereign debt but sterling stole the limelight as it fell to seven-year lows for the third consecutive day against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The pound shed about two cents on the day against the dollar, undermined by speculation that British rates would stay on hold in coming months amid benign inflation and broad dollar gains. \par \par \uc2  The dollar also gained ground against the yen amid wariness of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Such concern helped the euro to trim losses from recent record lows against the yen. \par \par \uc2  Wariness of such action was also the greater as European Union finance ministers (Ecofin) met near Paris, with the euro on their agenda. \par \par \uc2  "There is a risk of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and there is uncertainty in the background ahead of Ecofin meeting so traders are hitting sterling as it looks less risky," said Stephen Lewis, chief economist at Monument Derivatives. \par \par \uc2  "Sterling broke through $1.4350 decisively and on the way touched off a lot of technical business and the market is going to continue selling it until they find a technical support level. The $1.4075 level is important in that respect." \par \par \uc2  Sterling hit a trough of $1.4204, its lowest level since February 1993, while euro/sterling rose about a penny on the day. The pound even fell against the otherwise retreating yen to hit five-year lows. \par \par \uc2  DOLLAR PROFITS FROM JAPAN DOWNGRADE \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the dollar was hovering nearly a yen above two-month lows near 104.75 yen set a day ago. It gained after Moody's Investors Service downgraded Japan's sovereign debt to Aa2 from Aa1. \par \par \uc2  The yen came under further pressure after data showed an 11.7 percent slide in Japan's machinery orders in July from the previous month. \par \par \uc2  "The downgrade was not a surprise but nonetheless it does does not help the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , especially when we had weak machinery orders data," said Audrey-Childe Freeman, economist at CIBC World Markets. \par \par \uc2  The euro was holding about a yen above Thursday's record lows around 90.90. It was up about a cent from Thursday's record lows around $0.8630. \par \par \uc2  Senior Finance Ministry official Zembei Mizoguchi said the recent rise in the yen was too rapid and added Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa has ordered ministry officials to act against such advances in Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The price action in euro/yen has been scrutinised by Japanese officials," said Mark Henry, strategist at GNI. \par \par \uc2  "With (Japanese) GDP figures out on Monday, there is a very good chance the BOJ will step into the market then to get euro/yen higher and 90 will be defended." \par \par \uc2  Wariness as euro-zone finance ministers (Ecofin) gathered for a three-day meeting helped keep the euro a cent above this week's record lows against he dollar. \par \par \uc2  "Most people are not expecting anything but some people think there is a 10 percent chance that they (ECB) would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Lewis from Monument Derivatives. \par \par \uc2  "If we come back on Monday and nothing has happened, the euro will resume its natural direction." \par \par \uc2  German sources said on Thursday euro-zone finance ministers planned a statement at the talks on Friday to push home the message that the euro was out of line with fundamentals. \par \par \uc2  However, they said it was unlikely the statement by the so-called Euro Group - comprising the 11 members of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  union plus Greece, which will join next year - would refer to \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The euro's rise to the day's highs coincided with comments from the ECB's Executive Board member Sirkka Hamalainen who said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had not overreacted to short-term developments when setting interest rates and that it was not happy with the euro's value on the foreign exchanges. \par \par \uc2  The euro briefly fell back as traders focused on a Spanish newspaper El Mundo report that European Monetary Affairs Commissioner Pedro Solbes had said the ECB should not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the euro but focus on inflation. But EU spokesman denied Solbes said the ECB should not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Traders are now awaiting comments from ECB President Wim Duisenberg who is scheduled to speak on the "International role of the euro" at 1530 GMT in Calgary. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw9808i36\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
