\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen soft after Japan downgrade, euro eyes Ecofin. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Carolyn Cohn \par \uc2 538 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 September 2000\par 10:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Sept 8 (Reuters) - The yen eased against the dollar and the euro following a downgrade of Japan's sovereign debt on Friday, but the euro/dollar rate held above this week's record lows as euro zone finance ministers meet. \par \par \uc2  Fear of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  also played a strong part in weakening the yen and strengthening the euro, analysts said, ahead of Japanese GDP data to be released in Tokyo on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Moody's Investors Service downgraded Japan's sovereign debt to Aa2 from Aa1 in a widely anticipated move. The yen was also undermined by data showing an 11.7 percent slide in Japan's machinery orders in July from the previous month. \par \par \uc2  But the impact was likely to be short-lived, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "The effect of the downgrade was only temporary," said Nick Parsons, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Commerzbank in London. \par \par \uc2  "The market is not really being driven by any real assessment of fundamentals, but by psychology," he added. \par \par \uc2  The yen's performance marked a turnaround from a two-month high near 104.75 struck against the dollar and record highs beyond 91 set against the euro on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The yen was trading around 105.50 to the dollar and 92 to the euro at 0700 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Senior Finance Ministry official Zembei Mizoguchi, meanwhile, said the recent rise in the yen was too rapid, and added Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa has ordered ministry officials to act against such advances in Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The price action 