\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Fainthearted euro hits record low vs dollar, yen. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Carolyn Cohn \par \uc2 767 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 September 2000\par 14:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Sept 7 (Reuters) - The euro fell to its lowest in its 20-month life against the dollar and yen on Thursday, as sentiment turned increasingly sour over the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's prospects amid conflicting comments from European officials. \par \par \uc2  Broad dollar strength propelled the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to two-year highs against the Australian dollar, within sight of record peaks, even though London traders spotted the Reserve Bank of Australia buying its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for U.S. dollars. \par \par \uc2  Differing remarks by European officials on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's current levels has dented confidence in the euro, analysts said. It was also seen suffering because U.S. growth, currently running above 5 percent, contrasts with the euro zone, which is growing at about 3-1/2 percent, they added. \par \par \uc2  "The primary reason for euro weakness remains the story of U.S. growth, while we have had a few soft numbers on European growth recently, said David Brickman, international economist at PaineWebber. \par \par \uc2  Brickman added that contradictory comments from European policy-makers had also hurt the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's credibility. \par \par \uc2  The euro fell below 91 yen EURJPY=) for the first time, marking the third successive day of record lows. It also dropped below $0.8640 EUR=) to hit record troughs for the second straight day, according to Reuters data. \par \par \uc2  The scale of the euro's slide against the yen succeeded in driving the dollar to two-month lows against the yen. \par \par \uc2  But the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  enjoyed broad gains against other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , climbing to multi-year peaks against sterling, the New Zealand dollar and the Swiss franc. \par \par \uc2  It appreciated as far as US$0.5535 AUD=) against the Australian dollar, even after the RBA was spotted buying its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in London. An RBA official in London declined to comment on its market activities. The dollar also reached an historic high beyond $0.42 NZD=) against the New Zealand dollar. \par \par \uc2  SCHROEDER GETS THE BLAME \par \par \uc2  Analysts said German Chancellor Gerhard Schroeder played a leading role in the euro's two cent slide on Wednesday after his office repeated his lack of concern with the euro's weakness. \par \par \uc2  Schroeder later backpedalled, saying the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's trend was "unpleasant" and that its level did not reflect the economic might of Europe. But by then the euro had already been sucked into a whirl of sell orders. \par \par \uc2  The German Finance Ministry tried to prop up the euro on Thursday, by saying that Germany was "eminently interested" in a strong euro and that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had strong upward potential. \par \par \uc2  France and Germany also said euro zone finance ministers were planning to issue a statement on the euro at their meeting on Friday, after French and German finance ministers discussed the weak euro on the telephone. \par \par \uc2  The European Commission, meanwhile, said the euro's current level was "not appropriate". \par \par \uc2  But analysts and dealers said Schroeder's conflicting remarks and the fact that the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was silent on its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's woes had left the euro at the mercy of speculative attacks. \par \par \uc2  "It's distress selling," said a trader at a Japanese bank. \par \par \uc2  "We were at $0.89 yesterday and are down nearly three big figures, so people are nervous." \par \par \uc2  The euro found no support from French second quarter GDP data, which showed below-forecast growth of 0.7 percent. \par \par \uc2  The yen's strength against the euro fed into gains against the dollar, which fell one percent on the day to two-month lows near 105 JPY=) against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Senior \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  official Zembei Mizoguchi said on Thursday that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to halt the yen's rise against the euro. \par \par \uc2  "As far as BOJ (Bank of Japan) and MOF (\b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) are concerned, neither of them are happy," said Jeremy Hawkins, chief economic adviser at Bank of America in London. \par \par \uc2  "It's getting to the stage that if the ECB wanted to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the BOJ is looking like a good candidate (for joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 )." \par \par \uc2  In Europe, the dollar stood tall against the Swiss franc CHF=), hurdling 11-year highs above 1.79 francs. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also hit seven-year highs against sterling GBP=) ahead of the Bank of England's decision to leave its key repo rate unchanged at 6.0 percent, as expected. \par \par \uc2  "British rates aren't far from their peak so I would expect sterling to slip against the dollar but still remain strong against the euro," Gerard Lyons, global head of treasury research at Standard Chartered, told Reuters Television. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw9708tij\par }\pag