\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Lovelorn euro hits record lows versus dollar, yen. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Carolyn Cohn \par \uc2 638 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 September 2000\par 12:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Sept 7 (Reuters) - The euro visited new historic lows against the dollar and the yen on Thursday, extending sharp losses of a day earlier as gloom about its outlook was exacerbated by conflicting remarks by European officials. \par \par \uc2  The euro fell below 91 yen in the European session, its weakest in its 20-month life, and plumbed depths below $0.8650, according to Reuters data. \par \par \uc2  The scale of the euro's slide against the yen succeeded in driving the dollar down to two-month lows against the yen but the dollar continued to hold near multi-year peaks against sterling, the Australian dollar, the New Zealand dollar and the Swiss franc. \par \par \uc2  With gloom rife about its prospects, more losses were seen on the cards. \par \par \uc2  "The euro story is not based on euro zone economic fundamentals," said Neil Parker, treasury economist at Royal Bank of Scotland. \par \par \uc2  "The euro has got further to fall." \par \par \uc2  Analysts said German Chancellor Gerhard Schroeder played a leading role in the euro's two cent slide on Wednesday after his office repeated his lack of concern with the euro's weakness. \par \par \uc2  Schroeder later backpedalled, saying the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's trend was "unpleasant" and that its level did not reflect the economic might of Europe. But by then the euro had already been sucked into a whirl of sell orders. "The German comments have been negative for the euro because people think that European officials are not taking the euro seriously," said Niels Christensen, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Societe Generale in Paris. \par \par \uc2  The German Finance Ministry tried to prop the euro on Thursday, by saying that Germany was "eminently interested" in a strong euro and that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had strong upward potential. \par \par \uc2  France and Germany also said euro zone finance ministers were planning to issue a statement on the euro at their meeting on Friday, after French and German finance ministers discussed the weak euro on the telephone. \par \par \uc2  But analysts and dealers said Schroeder's conflicting remarks and the fact that the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was silent on its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's woes had left the euro at the mercy of speculative attacks. \par \par \uc2  "It's distress selling," said a trader at a Japanese bank. \par \par \uc2  "We were at $0.89 yesterday and are down nearly three big figures, so people are nervous." \par \par \uc2  YEN CAPITALISES ON EURO WOES \par \par \uc2  The yen's strength against the euro fed into gains against the dollar, which fell one percent on the day to two-month lows against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Senior \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  official Zembei Mizoguchi said on Thursday that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to halt the yen's rise against the euro. \par \par \uc2  "As far as BOJ (Bank of Japan) and MOF (\b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) are concerned, neither of them are happy," said Jeremy Hawkins, chief economic adviser at Bank of America in London. \par \par \uc2  "It's getting to the stage that if the ECB wanted to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the BOJ is looking like a good candidate (for joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  The dollar fell as far as 105.15 yen by 0950 GMT, bucking its generally stronger trend. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  jumped to a two-year high around US$0.56 against the Australian dollar, despite talk in Sydney of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the Australian dollar by the Reserve Bank of Australia. It also leaped to an historic high near $0.42 against the New Zealand dollar. \par \par \uc2  The RBA in London declined to comment on its market activities when questioned by Reuters. \par \par \uc2  In Europe, the dollar stood tall against the Swiss franc, hurdling 11-year highs above 1.79 francs. \par \par \uc2  It also hit seven-year highs against sterling ahead of the Bank of England's monetary policy decision at 1100 GMT, where no change in rates is expected. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw9708sh6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
