\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Sagging euro mired near record lows vs dollar, yen. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Lisa Jucca \par \uc2 716 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 September 2000\par 09:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  (Updates throughout, adds quotes and latest prices, changes dateline and byline) \par \par \uc2  LONDON, Sept 7 (Reuters) - The euro hit new record lows against the dollar and the yen on Thursday, extending sharp losses posted a day earlier as gloom about its outlook was compounded by conflicting remarks by European officials. \par \par \uc2  The euro had weakened to life lows below $0.8650 and below 91.65 yen by early European trading. \par \par \uc2  The single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's losses were particularly hefty against the rampant dollar, which also surged to multi-year peaks against sterling, the Australian dollar, the New Zealand dollar and the Swiss franc. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said German Chancellor Gerhard Schroeder played a leading role in the euro's two cent slide on Wednesday after his office repeated his lack of concern with the euro's weakness. \par \par \uc2  Schroeder later backpedalled, saying the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's trend was "unpleasant" and that its level did not reflect the economic might of Europe. But by then the euro had already been sucked into a whirl of selling orders. \par \par \uc2  The German Finance Ministry tried to prop the euro on Thursday by saying that Germany was "eminently interested" in a strong euro and that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had strong upward potential. "The German comments have been negative for the euro because people think that European officials are not taking the euro seriously," said Niels Christensen, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Societe Generale in Paris. \par \par \uc2  "Right now no one wants to buy the euro and it's not only short-term players. Long-term investors are getting more and more nervous about the outlook for the euro." \par \par \uc2  Analysts said Schroeder's conflicting remarks and the fact that the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was silent on its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's woes had left the euro at the mercy of speculative attacks. \par \par \uc2  "The fact that (ECB's President Wim) Duisenberg did not mention the euro is surprising," said Christensen. \par \par \uc2  "It's probably an attempt not to lose credibility. In such a short market a strong statement would not turn the tide but could at least calm the market." \par \par \uc2  Dealers did not rule out however the possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  talk ahead of a meeting of euro zone finance ministers in Versailles, France, on Friday and said this could offer the euro some interim support. \par \par \uc2  "A few people were shocked about the size of the move yesterday, but we'll see more of a consolidation today," said a dealer at a European bank in London. \par \par \uc2  "I would not be surprised to see it up a touch." \par \par \uc2  Senior Minstry of Finance official Zembei Mizoguchi said on Thursday that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to halt the yen's rise against the euro. \par \par \uc2  DOLLAR POWERS AHEAD \par \par \uc2  The dollar was strong across the board, jumping to a fresh two-year high of around US$0.56 against the Australian dollar before pulling back on talk of Reserve Bank of Australia's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It leaped to a historic high near $0.42 against the New Zealand dollar. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the Australian dollar was pressured by selling against the yen by Japanese exporters before getting a lift amid talk of RBA \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The RBA is buying almost constantly through brokers around 56 cents," said a foreign bank dealer in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  The dollar stood tall against the Swiss franc, skidding to 11-year low of 1.7889 francs. It was also near seven-and-a-half-year highs against sterling. \par \par \uc2  "What we're seeing is the mighty dollar," said a dealer for a major city bank in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said recent U.S. economic data lessened concern that U.S. asset markets may be undermined by the need for Fed rate hikes in the near term and reinforced confidence in the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Unless such confidence fades, the dollar's tone seems likely to continue firm, they added. \par \par \uc2  The dollar stood at 106.17/27 yen against 105.87 yen in late U.S. trading on Wednesday, getting a mild lift from slightly weaker than expected capital spending numbers in the Japanese Finance Ministry's corporate survey for April-June. \par \par \uc2  The data showed capital spending up 2.2 percent year-on-year in April-June, off slightly from a 3.3 percent rise in January-March. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw9708fcc\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (japan near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw) and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority)\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\